{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek","id":1439351,"title":"Technocrats and Star Trek?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-03-11T19:31:07-08:00","id":1439351,"title":"Technocrats and Star Trek?","content":"I have another annoying question about the Technocracy. A few times I've seen them mentioned as the only option for playing hard-science Star Trek types. But...<br /> <br /> Star Trek is just about the mushiest, least consistent, least plausible scifi on TV. And The Federation is all about .... communism and the Prime Detective. It's even a multi-species collective.<br /> But the Void Engineers are capitalist space marines? Funded by the Syndicate. And... they shoot aliens instead of making alliances with them?<br /> And... isn't outer space literally in the Umbra? Doesn't that make hard sci-fi just not possible in-setting?<br /> <br /> Once again, I don't get it. Not saying it's badwrongfun, but <i>how</i> does it scratch that Star Trek itch?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T21:05:46-08:00","id":1439362,"title":"","content":"Well for starters you have to understand the Union's history from an out-of-game perspective. While the Technocracy was first positioned as the pure evil Bad Guys of MtAs in the beginning, the Void Engineers were different. They were seen as good guys, often dubbed the Star Trek Convention by fans as they were more interested in going out there and exploring. The VE were the hopeful, optimistic ones. They wanted Mankind to become like the Humans of Star Trek, that they were going to help them become that. Even their wayward Technocrat bothers and sisters.<br /> <br /> They were not just willing to work with Mages but other Supernaturals. In fact there was a lot speculation both in and out of universe until like five or six years ago that the VE were going to abandon the Technocracy and go independent. Then their Revised CB came out and the VE themselves flat out squashed any notion of them leaving.<br /> <br /> In fact, the darkest aspect of the original VE Convention book was that the first couple chapters featured a VE talking about the Conventions' history, it's outlook and all that to a some mages, a werewolf and a changeling, only to in the end reveal that she was Nephandi-tainted, implying that a number of the Convention was being co-opted by eldritch entities in the Far Umbra. The Rev Ed book straight out labels her as dangerous Nephandi and not to be trusted.<br /> <br /> It's the more recent developments that has seen the VE darken in their outlook, going from the Star Trek Convention to the NuBSG Convention. From a Convention of Scientists and Explorers with some military force on the side to a Convention of Soldiers with some science and exploration on the side. All because of the damage the Avatar Storm wrought upon them and the damage it continues to cause.<br /> <br /> One of the great tragedies of the Union is that their most hopeful and most optimistic Convention is slowly losing it all for simple survival and none outside the VE are aware of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T21:30:01-08:00","id":1439365,"title":"","content":"So they were really depicted as making friends <i>even with changelings and werewolves</i>? Yes, that is a surprise to me, but I can see how it feels Star Trek-y.<br /> <br /> But weren't the Void Engineers also waging space opera warfare against the Sons of Ether, Nephandi, and Marauders to rule the other planets? When they could have secretly teamed up with the Etherites to at least stop the Nephandi and Marauders and Threat Null out there... they decided to sacrifice all their own ideals instead?<br /> <br /> That doesn't seem like consistent writing about them being neutral to outsiders. And it doesn't really work with them begging the Euthanatoi to let them use Ravanna's Eye while planning to continue shooting their Etherite allies (and the Euthanatoi would know this because they can read minds). Or start shooting them if that's a new, Revised development. It also isn't all that consistent a depiction of their ideals mattering that much to them either, including the part about getting help from literal necromancers.<br /> <br /> And they unquestioningly, unanimously stick with the Union even knowing that they can't ever explain Threat Null because the allies they love would happily join Threat Null and help blow up their own voidships? But doesn't that.... uh.... bother them? I mean, I thought they were <i>terrified</i> of the rest of the Union becoming Threat Null. But that's not a sane reason to double down on helping them against the guys who could be their actual, genuine allies if they'd just swallow some pride. Do they believe the Etherites and Traditions were recently taken over by Nephandi or something?<br /> <br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, semi-magical space opera contests between Void Engineers and Sons of Ether actually sounds a lot more fun than Technocracy-as-Paranoia (to be fair, most things would). But I'm having trouble following the internal logic of their policies in any edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-12-2021, 12:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T21:51:22-08:00","id":1439370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek#post1439351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have another annoying question about the Technocracy. A few times I've seen them mentioned as the only option for playing hard-science Star Trek types. But...<br /> <br /> Star Trek is just about the mushiest, least consistent, least plausible scifi on TV. And The Federation is all about .... communism and the Prime Detective. It's even a multi-species collective.<br /> But the Void Engineers are capitalist space marines? Funded by the Syndicate. And... they shoot aliens instead of making alliances with them?<br /> And... isn't outer space literally in the Umbra? Doesn't that make hard sci-fi just not possible in-setting?<br /> <br /> Once again, I don't get it. Not saying it's badwrongfun, but <i>how</i> does it scratch that Star Trek itch?</div> </div> </div> </div>Take note that this is why the Void Engineers were supposed to defect.<br /> <br /> The VE wanted to be Star Trek and meet aliens.<br /> <br /> The rest of the Union wondered why the VE weren't acting more like Warhammer 40K.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But weren't the Void Engineers also waging space opera warfare against the Sons of Ether, Nephandi, and Marauders to rule the other planets? When they could have secretly teamed up with the Etherites to at least stop the Nephandi and Marauders and Threat Null out there... they decided to sacrifice all their own ideals instead? </div> </div> </div>Generally they WERE teaming against the Nephandi and Marauders with the Sons of Ether and more or less knew better than anyone else that &quot;different does not equal evil.&quot;<br /> <br /> Because the Void Engineers had DIMENSIONAL SCIENCE which means, through scientific gobbledegook terms:<br /> <br /> &quot;We summon and control spirits as well as make pacts with them.&quot;<br /> <br /> The reason why some wanted to defect was because of these alliances. Then like 90% of the Convention was killed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-12-2021, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T21:59:30-08:00","id":1439374,"title":"","content":"Yeah, killed by the Dimenional Anomaly they themselves created.<br /> <br /> But this helps clarify the 2E situation.<br /> <br /> The Threat Null also should have been a giant neon sign warning them to leave the Union <b>now</b> and run away as fast as possible. As you said, Threat Null is the ultimate creation of the Union itself. And the VEs even realize the other Conventions may voluntarily join them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-12-2021, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T22:02:59-08:00","id":1439375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439374#post1439374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, killed by the Dimenional Anomaly they themselves created.<br /> <br /> But this helps clarify the 2E situation.<br /> <br /> The Threat Null also should have been a giant neon sign warning them to leave the Union <b>now</b> and run away as fast as possible. As you said, Threat Null is the ultimate creation of the Union itself. And the VEs even realize the other Conventions may voluntarily join them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, the Void Engineer who dropped the nuke on the Labyrinth was a Nephandi.<br /> <br /> The Void Engineers are now also fighting Threat Null, which means they're explictly the good guys against the 1st Edition Technocracy on steroids.<br /> <br /> They don't defect NOW because the irony is that the Union's worst elements are people they can legally shoot and everyone else is off the Kool Aid too. M20's Technocracy guide shows the Unionists are like 1/10th the assholes they used to be.<br /> <br /> Which is still pretty assholish but not that much worse than the Traditions and they have Nukes and Hit Marks needed to fight the Borg and Daleks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T22:06:58-08:00","id":1439377,"title":"","content":"Yeah again, that was the VE <b><i>before</i></b> the Avatar Storm, before the Revised Edition. Prior to that, Threat Null didn't exist and the VE were thriving. Now, they're just trying to survive and keep the Earth safe, with some fleeting hopes of recovering what they lost.<br /> <br /> That said, even after it they're willing to work with the Traditions against the Nephandi, Threat Null and other horrors out in the void. In fact, they're just as likely to avoid fighting the Traditions in the void now than they did back then due to how battered and over-stretched they've become.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T22:11:57-08:00","id":1439379,"title":"","content":"It's also worth mentioning that Threat Null is capable of straight up assimilating membership of the other four Conventions whether said mages want it or not, via a turbocharged version of the indoctrination that they've undergone. Since the VE have been deprogrammed, they're relatively safe. But if they left, the Syndicate or ItX would start launching offworld projects, and only one has to come in contact with the Nulls to infect the entire earthbound Union. In a lot of ways, the Void Engineers want more than ever to leave Control and conditioning and the constant audits behind, but they've come to the grim realization that they're the thin membrane between the powderkeg that is their ostensible allies and the open flame that is their corrupted former leadership.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T22:16:48-08:00","id":1439380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439377#post1439377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah again, that was the VE <b><i>before</i></b> the Avatar Storm, before the Revised Edition. Prior to that, Threat Null didn't exist and the VE were thriving. Now, they're just trying to survive and keep the Earth safe, with some fleeting hopes of recovering what they lost.<br /> <br /> That said, even after it they're willing to work with the Traditions against the Nephandi, Threat Null and other horrors out in the void. In fact, they're just as likely to avoid fighting the Traditions in the void now than they did back then due to how battered and over-stretched they've become.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ascension War ended with Revised so the Void Engineers haven't been at war with the Traditions for decades. Literally, most modern VE probably have never fought in the Ascension War.<br /> <br /> The Progenitors and those crazy psycho brain stealing NWO are pretty much the only people continuing to do so.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T22:30:42-08:00","id":1439381,"title":"","content":"Nilbog hit it right on the head. The VE are terrified of the rest of the Union finding out about Threat Null and how they'll react to it. So they don't tell them. Even as ItX continues to demand expeditions to Autochthonia, they refuse to tell them. Even as they know the NWO knows they're hiding things from the rest of them, they refuse to tell them. Even as they beg the Syndicate for more funding and resources to fight Threat Null, they don't tell them. Even as the Progenitors notice the signs of PTSD and trauma growing among them, they refuse to tell them.<br /> <br /> So they stay and they fight. Traumatized by everything they've lost and by the fighting they still wage in the void to defend the Earth.<br /> <br /> Like I said, it's one of the great tragedies that the most hopeful and optimistic of them are slowly losing that hope and optimism, unseen and unnoticed by those around them all because of that fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T22:53:02-08:00","id":1439386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439381#post1439381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nilbog hit it right on the head. The VE are terrified of the rest of the Union finding out about Threat Null and how they'll react to it. So they don't tell them. Even as ItX continues to demand expeditions to Autochthonia, they refuse to tell them. Even as they know the NWO knows they're hiding things from the rest of them, they refuse to tell them. Even as they beg the Syndicate for more funding and resources to fight Threat Null, they don't tell them. Even as the Progenitors notice the signs of PTSD and trauma growing among them, they refuse to tell them.<br /> <br /> So they stay and they fight. Traumatized by everything they've lost and by the fighting they still wage in the void to defend the Earth.<br /> <br /> Like I said, it's one of the great tragedies that the most hopeful and optimistic of them are slowly losing that hope and optimism, unseen and unnoticed by those around them all because of that fear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly, it's when they're at their most aligned with the Union as well as morally justified.<br /> <br /> Mind you, while it will be a big blow, I don't actually think the modern Union would be THAT shocked by the argument, &quot;By the way, our former members were turned into monsters by the Borg.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's just a thing they've been taught to expect about the Umbra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T05:50:43-08:00","id":1439428,"title":"","content":"There is still a degree of &quot;No War Beyond the Line!&quot; with the VEs. Trads, Changelings, etc. that will stand with them against threats to the Earth are welcome ... in space. On Earth it remains different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T08:14:43-08:00","id":1439449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439380#post1439380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Ascension War ended with Revised so the Void Engineers haven't been at war with the Traditions for decades. Literally, most modern VE probably have never fought in the Ascension War.<br /> <br /> The Progenitors and those crazy psycho brain stealing NWO are pretty much the only people continuing to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Astro's right. While the War has greatly eased up post-Avatar Storm, especially beyond Earth, and the Union has completely ended their Pogroms, the Ascension War is still going on.<br /> <br /> And actually most NWO and Syndicate members are fine with that. While they are having their own issues with the Masses and the Consensus, they're pretty confident that they've managed to beat the Traditions through social manipulations, that they are dying relics of a bygone age. Sure, they're still around and causing problems but they're far cry from what they were and they've learned ways of undermining them in the eyes of the Consensus without firing shots. Or as the Syndicate put it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We love the Traditions. They\u2019re an endless supply of fantastic product ideas. </div> </div> </div>You know, once I didn't really care for the Syndicate. Then their Rev Ed book came out and I developed a fondness for those money-grubbing assholes. Turning your enemies' Beliefs into products for the Masses to get them to think of such things as childish and fictional while making more revenue for yourself is such a brilliant, asshole move.<br /> <br /> But yeah the NWO and Syndicate have largely taken the stance of fight them directly when and where they have to, subtly undermine them the rest of the time. It's cheaper and easier that way and lets them focus on other important tasks.<br /> <br /> It's the Progenitors, and even then more gung-ho members of Applied Sciences that want the Pogrom and open war back because they've become quite upset over the Anti-vaxxers, Faith Healers and pseudo-science that some of the Mages are pushing on the Masses.<br /> <br /> And honestly I can't blame them. When I see stories of children suffering or outright dying of things that could have been easily treated or prevented but weren't because of their parents' delusional beliefs, I get quite angry. I could only imagine how I'd feel if such people were being used by some of my enemies to attack me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439386#post1439386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oddly, it's when they're at their most aligned with the Union as well as morally justified.<br /> <br /> Mind you, while it will be a big blow, I don't actually think the modern Union would be THAT shocked by the argument, &quot;By the way, our former members were turned into monsters by the Borg.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's just a thing they've been taught to expect about the Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there's two other things that makes Threat Null scary for them. First they can almost instantly co-opt and take over Conditioned Technocrats. The opening and closing fiction of their Rev Ed book revolves around, with a VE crew dealing with a ItXer stowaway that ends with them coming into contact with the ItX Threat Null and the woman almost immediately gets taken over by Threat Null through her cybernetics, ending with the VE Captain putting a bullet in her brain.<br /> <br /> The problem with that is every other Convention uses Conditioning to varying degrees. It's an expected part of the Union. The VE don't. If they tell the others about Threat Null they will have to tell them about that and then they will have to explain to their peers why Threat Null wasn't able to take them over, leading to the VE explaining how they undo the Union's Conditioning and have been long before Threat Null.<br /> <br /> That's not going to make other Conventions happy. Mistrust towards the VE will grow, mistrust that has already been on the rise because of how secretive they've been. Some doubt their claims about Threat Null or worse, think the Convention has itself been co-opted and are trying to sabotage the rest of the Union.<br /> <br /> The second thing is the terrifying question of where is the VE Threat Null? Why haven't they seen the twisted version of themselves? They don't know and it's a quiet fear within the Convention because by their own admission if anything in Threat Null knew how best to fight the VE it would be their Threat Null counterparts. If they tell the rest of the Union about Threat Null, they're going to ask where their counterparts are and when the VE doesn't have an answer for them, the other Conventions are going to get suspicious, adding to the above mistrust.<br /> <br /> So the VE are stuck. They're getting worn down but they cannot tell the others why they need more help, more resources. If they do tell them why, it could cause all kinds of new problems for them, problems that could be fatal for the Convention and the entire planet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T10:09:50-08:00","id":1439469,"title":"","content":"This is all really informative, thanks.<br /> <br /> So the other Conventions have not at all stopped trying to genocide the Traditions and Reality Deviants, they just think they can do it more subtly now. I recall reading that they invaded and utterly destroyed the last traces of all the Tradition Horizon Realms, too.<br /> <br /> Is Threat Null constantly growing or are they actually defeatable? I can ask the same about space Nephandi, actually. Isn't there only a small, finite number of Sleepers out there available to assimilate/convert/invert?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-12-2021, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T10:20:30-08:00","id":1439474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439469#post1439469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Threat Null constantly growing or are they actually defeatable? I can ask the same about space Nephandi, actually. Isn't there only a small, finite number of Sleepers out there available to assimilate/convert/invert?</div> </div> </div> </div>Threat Null is in the Umbra so it could have a planet of billions of robot people but it wouldn't matter unless they can get across the Veil.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> Actually, they have a Dyson Sphere and Autochtonia so they DO have planets of billions of robot people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-12-2021, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T11:28:22-08:00","id":1439482,"title":"","content":"Fun extra, the Trads would understand and ally with the VE. But the Trads lack the cash and the alliance would draw extra fury from both the Union and the Disperates. So it would only bring down the VEs and the Trads quickly and leave Earth's defense to the Disperates (since the Union would be absorbed, the Marauders would be useless, and the Nephandi simply a pain). And the Disperates can cause trouble for the Trads but they can't do anything useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T11:39:43-08:00","id":1439483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439469#post1439469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the other Conventions have not at all stopped trying to genocide the Traditions and Reality Deviants, they just think they can do it more subtly now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically. But it's a complex situation.<br /> <br /> A few things.<br /> <br /> Since the ancient Masters are all but gone, a lot of the bad blood suddenly ceased to exist.<br /> *Younger Traditionalists don't see why they should sabotage the Technocracy, and risk getting murdered. Especially now that the Technocracy has misteriously stopped sending the killer robots.<br /> *Meanwhile a lot of Idealist Technocrats that really, really, want to make a better world - and were condemned to a low level rank, to make sure they weren't able to influence anything - suddenly got a promotion because, simply there isn't enough personel to fill the ranks. These see little reason to go murder the supernatural hippies (except when they do, like with the Progenitors that want to smash homeopathy)<br /> <br /> The Technocracy believes the Consensus will erase RD's , so why care? RD's are either in their way to extintion or are too weak to do anything.<br /> *Subverting the paradigms to make sure nobody can get power from them, and controling the Consensus are the priorities<br /> <br /> Neither the Traditions nor the Technocracy are in a shape to figth a whole lot. I would say that currently both are more concerned with rebuilding, and tackling long lasting internal issues.<br /> *The Hit-Mark program had a huge setback because many facilities that made them were off world. There are many pogrom-loving Technocrats working on it, but I think it has yet to return to the times of MECHA<br /> *With the masters and the Realms, the Traditions also lost a lot of the firepower they could have mustered otherwise<br /> <br /> The Ascension War, however, it's not going to stop. The amount of mages trying to ash each other diminished compared with the wars arround the moons of jupiter, but the factions are very much active and pushing their agendas for reality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I recall reading that they invaded and utterly destroyed the last traces of all the Tradition Horizon Realms, too. </div> </div> </div>They did a number on some important Tradition Horizon Realms (Doisstetep / Horizon, the Realm), but the Storm probably caused more damage overall.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is Threat Null constantly growing or are they actually defeatable? I can ask the same about space Nephandi, actually. Isn't there only a small, finite number of Sleepers out there available to assimilate/convert/invert? </div> </div> </div>As <i>CTPhipps</i> said. They're a very Umbra based treath.<br /> <br /> Their numbers don't need to be limited by how many ppl can awaken in the sense that they can have allies and constructs that are purely otherworldly.<br /> <br /> Like, Nephandi have their patrons and the minions of their patrons. That may make them undefeatable in the Deep Umbra or certain Hells, much like how Malfeas it's undefeatable. But their ability to affect Earth it's limited w/o actual flesh &amp; bone agents (prefferably that wouldn't blow up in Paradox after entry). And that's why they're always trying to summon Cthulhu<br /> <br /> It's unclear how defeatable it's Treath Null in the Umbra. Threat Null may have resources to get more spirit robot people, perhaps beyond merely &quot;assimilatting&quot; earthers - but it's possible they depend on the technowizards for most of their opperation. That would make their numbers limited (at least to some extent), but even then there's also the thing that since they're spirits, they Reform unless really potent magick it's applied so they don't<br /> <br /> It's clear that defeating Treath Null isn't something that VE can do in their actual state by themselves, but they could be defeatable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-12-2021, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T12:26:41-08:00","id":1439494,"title":"","content":"Indeed. Aleph has the right of it. For example, several of the Rev Ed CBs express surprise and frustration that the Garou are still around as they had predicted them dying off years ago. And even before the Avatar Storm, there was a growing sense of 'We've won' among the Conventions. The RDs are dying off. There's no reason to waste resources on every last one of them when they're going to die off naturally. Just focus on the most dangerous and troublesome of them.<br /> <br /> There also something Aleph missed in their comments, the Nephandi. M20 and the Rev Ed CBs have been really pushing the idea of the Nephandi as the Real Antagonists of the setting. It's even one of the reasons why several of the Crafts formed the Disparate Alliance, to combat the spread of the Nephandi that the Technocracy and the Traditions have largely been blind to.<br /> <br /> For the Technocracy, they're also the problem of Nephandi infiltration they're trying to deal while also having to deal with the Nephandi outside the Union. So they also have that on top of everything else Aleph mentioned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T13:03:41-08:00","id":1439500,"title":"","content":"Isnt NWO kinda &quot;communist&quot; and it brings them at odds with the syndicate? <br /> <br /> Star trek is the technocratic dream they want to make into reality. <br /> The Umbra is not where you find intelligent life. It's where you find spirit immitations. Should the earth actually find aliens from the material plane, the technocracy will want to extend its hand in peace and friendship, unless of course these aliens are space witches in which case whole planets gotta burn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T14:09:01-08:00","id":1439511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439500#post1439500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isnt NWO kinda &quot;communist&quot; and it brings them at odds with the syndicate?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Russian NWO was at odds with the American NWO over it but the American NWO won.<br /> <br /> The Union would be having more civil wars like they had during WW2 if not for the Traditions to unite them against.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-12-2021, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T11:16:44-08:00","id":1439689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439500#post1439500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isnt NWO kinda &quot;communist&quot; and it brings them at odds with the syndicate?</div> </div> </div> </div>This idea comes from the Syndiate book, but it can be misleading: It's true that in the cases where NWO agents bother to learn Hypereconomics/Primal Utility, they tend to err towards focusin on public institutions, rather than private business.<br /> <br /> NWO it's about controling society trough it's institutions, that's why they're the alphabet agencies, the creepy advisors to the power...It's obvious they will care about the economic plans of the state, and state owned institutions - caring about these it's their job.<br /> <br /> Normaly they won't worry a lot for the economy in general, because the Syndicate it's supposed to be controling the economy - aren't they? - only when they suspect Syndicate it's doing a bad job (there's a crisis, and we at the White Tower weren't ordering one :P - remember these books were written not much after 2008 crisis), it's when they start to take matters in their own hands.<br /> <br /> Comunism or Socialism, understood as systems opposed to Capitalism, fall mostly under the umbrella of &quot;economy&quot;. NWO may be passionate about some social structures that exist under those systems, but I would say they in general don't care a whole lot for the <i>economical</i> aspects of Control...The only Technocrats I see as clearly passionate about Socialism vs. Capitalism are those Syndicate agents that go roge, try to change the world, and usually either get back to the Syndicate disillusioned, or join the Etherites","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T11:24:40-08:00","id":1439692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439689#post1439689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This idea comes from the Syndiate book, but it can be misleading: It's true that in the cases where NWO agents bother to learn Hypereconomics/Primal Utility, they tend to err towards focusin on public institutions, rather than private business.<br /> <br /> NWO it's about controling society trough it's institutions, that's why they're the alphabet agencies, the creepy advisors to the power...It's obvious they will care about the economic plans of the state, and state owned institutions - caring about these it's their job.<br /> <br /> Normaly they won't worry a lot for the economy in general, because the Syndicate it's supposed to be controling the economy - aren't they? - only when they suspect Syndicate it's doing a bad job (there's a crisis, and we at the White Tower weren't ordering one :P - remember these books were written not much after 2008 crisis), it's when they start to take matters in their own hands.<br /> <br /> Comunism or Socialism, understood as systems opposed to Capitalism, fall mostly under the umbrella of &quot;economy&quot;. NWO may be passionate about some social structures that exist under those systems, but I would say they in general don't care a whole lot for the <i>economical</i> aspects of Control...The only Technocrats I see as clearly passionate about Socialism vs. Capitalism are those Syndicate agents that go roge, try to change the world, and usually either get back to the Syndicate disillusioned, or join the Etherites</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the info.<br /> <br /> I am not familiar with the lore and the command chain of the Technocracy, who is on charge of the organization as a whole Syndicate, NWO or another faction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T11:54:38-08:00","id":1439696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439692#post1439692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the info.<br /> <br /> I am not familiar with the lore and the command chain of the Technocracy, who is on charge of the organization as a whole Syndicate, NWO or another faction?</div> </div> </div> </div>The NWO -more specifically, the White Tower - sets the policy of the Union. So, it could be said they're the ones in charge.<br /> <br /> But the Syndicate has a lot of informal power because they distribute the resources of the Union (Quint, money, etc...), and you can't do much w/o these<br /> <br /> This is the <b>real </b>source of conflict between them, more than any ideology or policy. NWO want's to do X but the Syndicate would rather allocate resources on Y","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T12:08:04-08:00","id":1439700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439692#post1439692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not familiar with the lore and the command chain of the Technocracy, who is on charge of the organization as a whole Syndicate, NWO or another faction?</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, that's a question. The Technocracy's command structure, outside each Convention's internal organisation, is by rank, at least insofar as the Technocrats in question are still concerned with Earthly affairs. Beyond that, well... they'd prefer not to draw the attention of the Masters of the Technocracy who dwell in the Deep Umbra, looking to avoid the Paradox that would come with use of their full Enlightened authority.<br /> <br /> Who's ultimately at the top of the pyramid - and even <i>if</i> there's anyone ultimately in charge - is down to ST discretion, per Technocracy Reloaded.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: On the Earthly scale, however, Aleph's answer holds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T12:41:13-08:00","id":1439703,"title":"","content":"On the subject of economies in Sci Fi and how the NWO might respond to them, please remember the NWO isn't dumb. They can be described as fanatics or fools (I'd say both) but neither ignorant nor stupid. They'd have to know that a suficiantly advanced technology combined with a functional government would make Capitalism nonfunctional. In a world of teleporters, replicators, robots (not Data but implied elsewhere), and cheap fusion power, most human physical labor would be worthless. The narrow elite would labor and the others would be on the dole. <br /> <br /> This appeals to the NWO as a means of control. The Hermetics, Etherites, Adepts, and Cultists see the same thing as a profound chance to grow and explore the self. They have different ideas about how to explore the self, wildly different, but they agree to disagree. Some Choristers also see the same things offering humanity time for prayer a d devotion. The other Trads have more mixed views.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T12:51:12-08:00","id":1439706,"title":"","content":"It's the Ivory Tower, not the White Tower. The White Tower of Languedoc was the original meeting hall for the leadership of the Order of Reason before it was destroyed in the 1700s.<br /> <br /> The Ivory Tower is Methodology (or faction) within the NWO that while possessing a great deal of influence within the Convention is technically not the leadership of the Convention. In fact, post-Avatar Storm, the Head of the Operatives has been placed as the defacto head of the Convention, mostly due his position and they were reluctant to put him on the Global Symposium, the replacement leadership council they've put together with the loss of Control.<br /> <br /> It's technically just called the Symposium but the term has also long been used for local and regional cross-Convention leadership councils. Like the local Technocrats of a city will answer to that city's symposium which will in turn report the national symposium, on and on all the way up to Control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T14:18:32-08:00","id":1439720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek#post1439351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have another annoying question about the Technocracy. A few times I've seen them mentioned as the only option for playing hard-science Star Trek types. But...<br /> <br /> Star Trek is just about the mushiest, least consistent, least plausible scifi on TV. And The Federation is all about .... communism and the Prime Detective. It's even a multi-species collective.<br /> But the Void Engineers are capitalist space marines? Funded by the Syndicate. And... they shoot aliens instead of making alliances with them?<br /> And... isn't outer space literally in the Umbra? Doesn't that make hard sci-fi just not possible in-setting?<br /> <br /> Once again, I don't get it. Not saying it's badwrongfun, but <i>how</i> does it scratch that Star Trek itch?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say one element of Star Trek that is strong with the Void Engineers is the presumption that Enlightement values are superior to Romantic values, and the need to teach others that this is true. Really, how many times has Star Trek encountered something superstitious or exhibiting old fashioned values, preached science and Enlightenment values to the offenders, and been proven right by the end of the episode, where the Romanticism valuing character either gets converted or dies for their sins against scientific thinking?<br /> <br /> Star Trek comes down firmly on the Enlightenment side of the Enlightenment vs Romanticism trope. That makes it very Technocratic despite its soft science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T09:39:18-07:00","id":1439826,"title":"","content":"My take on Threat Null: <br /> <br /> As others have pointed out, Threat Null was created by the Avatar Storm, and the surviving VEs shifted from Star Trek to BSG in response. But also note that Threat Null officially only has four factions, corresponding to Iteration X, the Progenitors, the NWO, and the Syndicate. There's no known counterpart to the VEs. The official line on this is that the lack of Conditioning among VE Operatives protects them from being converted; and the manuscript for Technocracy Reloaded suggests that those who <i>do</i> get converted become something that's difficult to distinguish from regular VEs: Sentinels who stand watch over the Earth against alien invaders. <br /> <br /> But I have a personal bit of head-canon, where many of the VEs who were lost to the Dimensional Anomaly didn't die. Instead, they became Explorers: an extreme version of the pre-Anomaly VE stereotype where they lost all interest in Earthly matters, abandoned the Technocracy, and went off exploring the Deep Universe and making friends with the aliens out there. They're not part of Threat Null in part because of their lack of Conditioning (which lead the other four Conventions' counterparts into having an alliance of sorts) and in part because they're not at this point a threat to Earth: they're too busy exploring to bother with Earth. <br /> <br /> But that has the potential to change: if the Explorers ever find that they need something from Earth (like its Nodes), they may end up coming back, leading an alliance of aliens that's exceptionally well-coordinated and well informed about Earth and the inner workings of Earth's defenses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T10:22:40-07:00","id":1439833,"title":"","content":"So about Threat Null:<br /> <br /> Autopolitans are fallen Iteration Xers?<br /> Transhumanity are fallen Progenitors?<br /> Agents are ?<br /> Residents are ?<br /> <br /> My headcanon is that they are the Static equivalent of Nephandi. Instead of inverting their Avatars, their Avatars have been frozen or calcified in a way that makes them incapable of Seeking, Ascension, or Descension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T10:38:47-07:00","id":1439840,"title":"","content":"I stated in another thread I wish they were the Seers of the Throne's variant in Mage.<br /> <br /> Because we need a fascist brutal regime for the Traditions and other resistance group to make sense. A group of mages who are against Ascension and want to make 99.9999% of Humanity unawakened slaves to the .00001% is pretty believable.<br /> <br /> You'd have the Elder Abominations of Stasis on top and you'd have all the mages who serve them promised stock options, hookers, blow, and UNLIMITED POWER.<br /> <br /> I mean, seriously, no end of recruits from both sides.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T11:21:24-07:00","id":1439855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439833#post1439833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So about Threat Null:<br /> <br /> Agents are ?<br /> Residents are ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Agents are NWO, Residents are Syndicate.<br /> There are *supposedly* no Threat Null Void Engineers - supoooosedly. It is a mystery wether or not that's true. Because a scary truth might be that they already infiltrated earth, given the normal Void Engineer Convention's abilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439840#post1439840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because we need a fascist brutal regime for the Traditions and other resistance group to make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>We...have a good reason for them to continue existing.<br /> The Union does not need to actively go max Pogrom on everything Mage in order for the Traditions and other groups to continue their resistance. They formed *because* of being hunted like that, sure, but just because it now has turned to a bit more of a Cold War, doesn't mean that those groups would disband.<br /> <br /> Actually, they went from a state of being hunted to a state of being suppressed, with a message of &quot;Stay in line, keep your head down, or else.&quot;<br /> It's not much better, really - everything the mystic cults and practicioners stand for and believe in is still actively kept to the shadows, fringes. They can't more openly live their life. Any obvious recruitment meets action from the Union. Their very beliefs are in the truest sense oppressed by the Union's watchful eye.<br /> <br /> I consider the current state more realistic than a cliche'd <i>&quot;There is SUCH A BIG EVIL that we gotta do something&quot;</i>. Reallife does not require an absolute evilest of cliche evils for resistances and revolutions to form. It just needs people in power and other people who really, really don't like that fact they're running the joint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 03-14-2021, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T12:45:58-07:00","id":1439872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439855#post1439855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We...have a good reason for them to continue existing.<br /> The Union does not need to actively go max Pogrom on everything Mage in order for the Traditions and other groups to continue their resistance. They formed *because* of being hunted like that, sure, but just because it now has turned to a bit more of a Cold War, doesn't mean that those groups would disband.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and that lacks urgency as well as potentially a lot of good gameplay.<br /> <br /> Having a big bad to blow up in a session may be lazy storytelling but it's USEFUL storytelling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I consider the current state more realistic than a cliche'd <i>&quot;There is SUCH A BIG EVIL that we gotta do something&quot;</i>. Reallife does not require an absolute evilest of cliche evils for resistances and revolutions to form. It just needs people in power and other people who really, really don't like that fact they're running the joint. </div> </div> </div>I think anyone who looks at the last 20 years and says, &quot;Well, the people in power aren't ALL BAD&quot; is a position that is needed in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Its a power fantasy to punch Far Right fascists and corrupt politicians and megacorps in the face.<br /> <br /> But it's a FUN power fantasy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-14-2021, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T13:01:06-07:00","id":1439874,"title":"","content":"One thing about M20 is it it is deliberately more open in terms of how it works then the other x-20 game lines. The unofficial tagline is \u201cit's your game, do as you Will\u201d. <br /> <br /> With that in mind, Threat Null can be thought of as what happens when Control is severed from earth, and co-opts Conditioned Technocrats it finds in the Umbra to use as a reclamation force. So while I don't feel the same need to have the technocracy be an evil fascist regime, if you want that you can easily justify it by saying that Threat Null succeeds in its mission, and Control reestablishes its dominance over the Technocratic Union.<br /> <br /> or you could go with the notion that the Avatar Storm never happened in the first place, and Control was never isolated from Earth to begin with.<br /> <br /> It's your game. Do as you will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T13:10:05-07:00","id":1439877,"title":"","content":"It kind of feels like they are going with a World of Warcraft model, where the Horde and Alliance fight viciously over things that are really rather trivial in the greater scheme of things, while the real enemy is the Infernal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T13:42:17-07:00","id":1439882,"title":"","content":"And on that note: if you want to use Mage to punch right wingers in the face, you do you. Again, it's your game, do as you will. Personally though, I'm of the opinion that in today's world, there are far too many people on both sides of the divide who have a vested interest in demonizing the other side; and there are far too many people on both sides of the divide who think that they know everything, believe that the other guys are evil, and think that punching them in the face is more important than trying to find any sort of common ground. So I'm less likely to go for \u201cpunch guys in the face\u201d narratives (unless the guys in question are Nephandi), and more likely to go for \u201covercome hubris, resolve misunderstandings, and heal divides\u201d narratives (again, unless the others in question are Fallen).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T14:21:13-07:00","id":1439893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439877#post1439877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It kind of feels like they are going with a World of Warcraft model, where the Horde and Alliance fight viciously over things that are really rather trivial in the greater scheme of things, while the real enemy is the Infernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, that was always an interpretation of the Ascension War and explicit in Revised. The Revised take was that fighting over what KIND of magic was silly since it was all just a tool that didn't matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439882#post1439882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And on that note: if you want to use Mage to punch right wingers in the face, you do you. Again, it's your game, do as you will. Personally though, I'm of the opinion that in today's world, there are far too many people on both sides of the divide who have a vested interest in demonizing the other side; and there are far too many people on both sides of the divide who think that they know everything, believe that the other guys are evil, and think that punching them in the face is more important than trying to find any sort of common ground. So I'm less likely to go for \u201cpunch guys in the face\u201d narratives (unless the guys in question are Nephandi), and more likely to go for \u201covercome hubris, resolve misunderstandings, and heal divides\u201d narratives (again, unless the others in question are Fallen).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reminded of a conversation here where I talked about the Nazi rallies in Kentucky and how I hated them before a poster gave me a firm dressing down that Nazis were something I shouldn't call right wingers and that it was despicable I was demonizing my enemies that way. I then had to correct him that I was referring to actual Neo Nazis and that they were having actual rallies. There's more than enough actual fascists and terrorists to go around that you don't need to &quot;demonize&quot; people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-14-2021, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T14:26:08-07:00","id":1439894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439893#post1439893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, that was always an interpretation of the Ascension War and explicit in Revised. The Revised take was that fighting over what KIND of magic was silly since it was all just a tool that didn't matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem, of course, is that <i>they</i> don't see the differences as trivial. They're absolutely certain that whatever it is that they're fighting over is the single most important thing in the Ascension War.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T14:28:24-07:00","id":1439896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439894#post1439894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem, of course, is that <i>they</i> don't see the differences as trivial. They're absolutely certain that whatever it is that they're fighting over is the single most important thing in the Ascension War.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even as a die-hard ascension warrior, I tended to agree with Revised. However, it also was weird because I thought that was the basis of the Traditions vs. Technocracy conflict in the first place.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Traditions are about it NOT mattering. Science, Magic, Sex, Drugs, Blood, and Religion are all tools for Ascension vs. TECHNOLOGY OR BUST, PROLE.&quot;<br /> <br /> Revised made it much more morally ambiguous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-14-2021, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T14:45:06-07:00","id":1439900,"title":"","content":"Peace, love, and understanding are the highest of goals, but the paradox of tolerance puts a hard and impassible limit on carrying it out. &quot;Common ground&quot; isn't &quot;common&quot; unless it's actually about tolerance.<br /> <br /> Just as the Mysticks in Mage can never find common ground with Technocrats (excepting VEs, apparently) as long as their goals include Pogrom/genocide, cultural eradication/forced conversion, and dictatorship. If the Mysticks and nonhuman sapients are still fighting just for their right to <i>exist</i>, they can't offer to make friends and shouldn't be expected to. Mysticks don't necessarily care about the rights of nonhumans, but they want to survive.<br /> <br /> The only way I can see the Technocracy having any genuine moral ambiguity (as an institution) is if they truly renounce the Pogrom as an ideological goal. Not just as an immediate, violent priority but as a concept to never try again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-14-2021, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T15:41:25-07:00","id":1439906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439877#post1439877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It kind of feels like they are going with a World of Warcraft model, where the Horde and Alliance fight viciously over things that are really rather trivial in the greater scheme of things, while the real enemy is the Infernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is certainly the stance M20 favors. The Nephandi are the Big Bad that the Traditions and Conventions have forgotten about in their own feud with each other.<br /> <br /> And it's certainly less frustrating than WoW has become.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439894#post1439894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem, of course, is that <i>they</i> don't see the differences as trivial. They're absolutely certain that whatever it is that they're fighting over is the single most important thing in the Ascension War.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah in MtAs, Belief is <u><i><b>EVERYTHING</b></i></u>. We can say that Tradition/Technocracy Conflict is in the end pointless because we are privy to knowledge that very, very few Mages ever discover and does that do are seldom in a position to share that knowledge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T15:46:08-07:00","id":1439908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439900#post1439900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Peace, love, and understanding are the highest of goals, but the paradox of tolerance puts a hard and impassible limit on carrying it out. &amp;quot;Common ground&amp;quot; isn't &amp;quot;common&amp;quot; unless it's actually about tolerance.<br /> <br /> Just as the Mysticks in Mage can never find common ground with Technocrats (excepting VEs, apparently) as long as their goals include Pogrom/genocide, cultural eradication/forced conversion, and dictatorship. If the Mysticks and nonhuman sapients are still fighting just for their right to <i>exist</i>, they can't offer to make friends and shouldn't be expected to. Mysticks don't necessarily care about the rights of nonhumans, but they want to survive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. But there's always the danger that you only <i>think</i> that someone is intolerant, possibly due to having fallen for propaganda yourself. To me, that's a big part of the horror of <i>Mage</i>: the Hubris. Everyone is so cock sure that they are in the right that it becomes far too easy to rationalize violence and oppression in the name of tolerance: \u201c<i>they're</i> the intolerant ones, so let's squash them like bugs!\u201d at the very least has built-in irony. <br /> <br /> And even if the other side does consist almost exclusively of liars and dupes (which I never take as a given without first thoroughly vetting the issue), is punching a dupe in the face really the best way to go? You might argue that you don't have much of a choice, because they're doing bad things and need to be stopped. But is that actually true, or is it just another rationale? Might it be possible to get through to the dupe and get him to change his mind? (Of course, <i>that</i> way potentially lies the equivalent of Room 101, if you're <i>so</i> sure he's in the wrong that re-education is warranted. Be careful when fighting monsters that you don't become one yourself.)<br /> <br /> In terms of the Technocracy and the Pogrom, how would you know? We've been told that they stopped the Pogrom in MRev for logistical reasons, not out of ethical concerns; but if they had stopped out of purely ethical concerns (\u201cthe guys who were in favor of the Pogrom are gone! Now we can stop that nonsense!\u201d), would the result have looked any different, in character? I don't think it would. <br /> <br /> And what if the justification is a mixture of ethics and logistics? How <i>much</i> of it needs to be ethics-based before you can accept that the Technocracy may not be evil monsters anymore? And again, how would you <i>know</i> what their reasons are? Are you going to break into various Constructs, abduct the Technocrats there, and mind-scan them in order to get a representative sample of what their motives were? That would be both impractical and unethical. <br /> <br /> So is it okay for the Traditions to automatically assume that the Technocracy is still evil after the Pogrom ends, or is that merely an understandable but still wrong assumption for them to make?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T15:49:57-07:00","id":1439909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439906#post1439906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is certainly the stance M20 favors. The Nephandi are the Big Bad that the Traditions and Conventions have forgotten about in their own feud with each other.<br /> <br /> And it's certainly less frustrating than WoW has become.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah in MtAs, Belief is <u><i><b>EVERYTHING</b></i></u>. We can say that Tradition/Technocracy Conflict is in the end pointless because we are privy to knowledge that very, very few Mages ever discover and does that do are seldom in a position to share that knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, M20 <i>hasn't</i> established that the traditions and technocracy have put their feud aside. Again, it's your game, do as you will. That includes whether or not the traditions and technocracy are at each other's throats or in some sort of detente.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T15:53:46-07:00","id":1439911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439909#post1439909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, M20 <i>hasn't</i> established that the traditions and technocracy have put their feud aside. Again, it's your game, do as you will. That includes whether or not the traditions and technocracy are at each other's throats or in some sort of detente.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the 20th Anniversaries are metaplot agnostic for the most part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T16:02:15-07:00","id":1439913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439911#post1439911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well the 20th Anniversaries are metaplot agnostic for the most part.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. The closest it gets to metaplot is the New Council of Magick, the introduction of the Disparate Alliance, and the hints at an upcoming reorganization of the Union and a purging of its reformist factions. None of that is presented as \u201cthis <i>will</i> happen\u201d or \u201cthis <i>has</i>happened\u201d; but there's a strong implication that if M20 <i>wasn't</i> metaplot-agnostic, this would be the new status quo. <br /> <br /> But it <i>is</i> metaplot-agnostic; so\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T16:04:47-07:00","id":1439915,"title":"","content":"A case can also be made that, like &quot;The Boys&quot;, Mage is basically a story about a corrupt Establishment versus a bunch of ruthless Terrorists. No matter which one wins, normal people lose. Sure, the Boys may be more sympathetic than the Seven because they are underdogs, but these are still people willing to blow up babies. Now technically &quot;The Boys&quot; fit mechanically more with Aberrant, of course, but the theme of Establishment vs Terrorists is common in almost all White Wolf books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T16:24:51-07:00","id":1439922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439915#post1439915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A case can also be made that, like &quot;The Boys&quot;, Mage is basically a story about a corrupt Establishment versus a bunch of ruthless Terrorists. No matter which one wins, normal people lose. Sure, the Boys may be more sympathetic than the Seven because they are underdogs, but these are still people willing to blow up babies. Now technically &quot;The Boys&quot; fit mechanically more with Aberrant, of course, but the theme of Establishment vs Terrorists is common in almost all White Wolf books.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the World of Darkness take on the subject. Honestly, I actually think it's more interesting to present the Traditionalists that way.<br /> <br /> But I don't think the Traditionalists ever were portrayed as terrorists.<br /> <br /> It was pretty black and white at the start but while the Union got better, I don't think the Traditions ever got worse. The worst they were ever portrayed was the House of Helekar and Revised had that group purged.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-14-2021, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T16:28:55-07:00","id":1439925,"title":"","content":"The first three editions were from their perspective; and very few people consider <i>themselves</i> to be terrorists. But yeah; even M20 doesn't call them terrorists, even though it doesn't paint as rosy a picture of them as previous editions did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T16:31:01-07:00","id":1439927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439906#post1439906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah in MtAs, Belief is <u><i><b>EVERYTHING</b></i></u>. We can say that Tradition/Technocracy Conflict is in the end pointless because we are privy to knowledge that very, very few Mages ever discover and does that do are seldom in a position to share that knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>At what scale is it pointless, though, and for whom? If a cabal/amalgam/whoever is minding their own business in their neighborhood, doing something innocuous and harmless like giving food to the homeless, and some other amalgam/cabal/whoever suddenly jumps them and blows up their chantry/construct/underground lair.... the attack was almost certainly pointless, but the guys being attacked have every reason to fight for their own lives. In the larger scheme, if it's entirely cosmically possible for multiple forms of magic and technology to all simultaneously exist and be believed in and work alongside one another, like in Starfinder, then there's no real reason for the Traditions and Technocrats to keep fighting each other. Except over all kinds of other things like democracy, or freedom of thought/thought crimes, or whether it's ethically justified to Gilgul Nephandi, or kill or enslave all the faeries everywhere. It's hard for me to believe the consensual reality is so fluid that ultimately nothing matters.<br /> <br /> What doesn't matter is how people achieve Ascension, right? But what if some Mages say... &quot;Wait a minute, if all of humanity Ascends then the universe will dissolve into chaos and/or cosmic violence! We have to stop this!&quot; and then you get people who are against the very idea of mass Ascension.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439908#post1439908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right. But there's always the danger that you only <i>think</i> that someone is intolerant, possibly due to having fallen for propaganda yourself. To me, that's a big part of the horror of <i>Mage</i>: the Hubris. Everyone is so cock sure that they are in the right that it becomes far too easy to rationalize violence and oppression in the name of tolerance: \u201c<i>they're</i> the intolerant ones, so let's squash them like bugs!\u201d at the very least has built-in irony.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is why they need diplomatic relations, so they can <i>attempt</i> to talk. If one side says &quot;Stop killing us! Stop taking away our voting rights!&quot; and the other guys say &quot;No, convert or die!&quot; or produce some dog-whistle* crap that amounts to the same, well then they still have a war no matter what they call it. If they respond with &quot;Stop blowing up our XYZ factories!&quot; then you can hope there's room for actual dialogue. Or at least try.<br /> <br /> Of course, nobody knows if the other guys' diplomats are lying or using illusions or who, precisely, they speak for within their larger group - nor if their faction will be unseated in some election/coup/bizarre magical accident next month. And everyone has to worry about their own diplomats being mind-controlled or possessed or replaced with clones or thrown in the Cauls on the way back home.<br /> <br /> The added difficulty is that if the leaders of both sides are still dead-set on war (even after the previous leaders all died), then their diplomats won't be reasonable, even if their underlings are generally less extreme.<br /> <br /> But the real underlying problem is if they actually <b>don't</b> really have any shared values, and both groups want to be the uncontested sole rulers of the world. The former seems fairly unlikely if <b>both</b> groups are large and diverse, but the latter... does seem to be true.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Dog-whistle isn't actually the word I'm looking for. I mean when someone tries to dissemble/hide/gaslight their hostile intent in some way, when talking to the person/group they want to hurt instead of to their own followers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439908#post1439908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of the Technocracy and the Pogrom, how would you know? We've been told that they stopped the Pogrom in MRev for logistical reasons, not out of ethical concerns; but if they had stopped out of purely ethical concerns (\u201cthe guys who were in favor of the Pogrom are gone! Now we can stop that nonsense!\u201d), would the result have looked any different, in character? I don't think it would.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, they wouldn't know IC. But if Mystick Mages and people who believe in their religions are squashed anytime they try to do anything besides hide with their heads down, they know the war isn't over.<br /> <br /> I think the key question is if group A is fighting group B over what they <b>are</b>, or over what they <b>do</b>. And if the As don't have the resources to target every single B, no it isn't possible to tell. And this being the WoD, the underdogs will be terrified and paranoid and probably assume the worst - especially in this case, where nobody seems to have anything really driving them to make peace. It's very, very hard for someone who has spent years being persecuted and traumatized, especially with their life constantly threatened, to let down that fear even if the pressure seems to be letting up. Every instinct screams to remain hyper-vigilant for the next attack. There'll still be that fear that it's only temporary, or even a ruse. And once group A has created that utter terror in group B, they've created hatred and fear that they can't easily fix even if they <b>do</b> decide to make peace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-14-2021, 08:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T19:50:05-07:00","id":1439963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439833#post1439833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So about Threat Null:<br /> <br /> Autopolitans are fallen Iteration Xers?<br /> Transhumanity are fallen Progenitors?<br /> Agents are ?<br /> Residents are ?<br /> <br /> My headcanon is that they are the Static equivalent of Nephandi. Instead of inverting their Avatars, their Avatars have been frozen or calcified in a way that makes them incapable of Seeking, Ascension, or Descension.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agents are NWO and Residents are Syndicate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T21:05:33-07:00","id":1439969,"title":"","content":"I had a thought about the VEs. I'm not sure if this is even plausible, but what they could really use to rebuild their numbers is to somehow make the COP a place where normal mortal humans can live and not become spirits. But I think I read somewhere that nobody born in &quot;space&quot; has Awakened, right?<br /> <br /> Even if it worked, how would they defend the COP? How did they ever defend it before? It's much bigger than Earth and has no Horizon. Whatever spells banished the Nephandi from Earth doesn't protect the COP either.<br /> <br /> And then I thought about my earlier question of whether there is a finite 'supply' of humans in space to become Nephandi or Threat Null. What if they can reproduce?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T21:14:32-07:00","id":1439972,"title":"","content":"Void Ships are apparently able to maintain an Earth-like environment by tethering themselves to a Node on Earth apparently, that link transfers the nature of the Earthly Foundations to the Void Ship and thus protects the crew from Void Adaptation. Or something to that effect. So you could theoretically do something likewise for COP, assuming it's still around. Though I'd tend to rule that the <i>size</i> of COP would be a problem here, and trying to import the Earthly Foundations to COP would be like trying to put out a first fire with a teaspoon of water. <br /> <br /> Another possibility would be to bring COP out of v the Umbra and into Conventional Space; the VEs have a Procedure for doing that sort of thing. But again, the COP is <i>huge</i>; I don't even want to think about how many successes would be needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T04:51:41-07:00","id":1440006,"title":"","content":"Why not have the Lost VE found a new culture in deep space. They could form a subtle threat. They don't want to destroy us or assimilate us, they want to save us.<br /> <br /> They would seem like friends to both the VEs and the Trads, and continue seeing themselves as friends even after their threat is understood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T05:02:03-07:00","id":1440008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439972#post1439972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Void Ships are apparently able to maintain an Earth-like environment by tethering themselves to a Node on Earth apparently, that link transfers the nature of the Earthly Foundations to the Void Ship and thus protects the crew from Void Adaptation. Or something to that effect. So you could theoretically do something likewise for COP, assuming it's still around. Though I'd tend to rule that the <i>size</i> of COP would be a problem here, and trying to import the Earthly Foundations to COP would be like trying to put out a first fire with a teaspoon of water.<br /> <br /> Another possibility would be to bring COP out of v the Umbra and into Conventional Space; the VEs have a Procedure for doing that sort of thing. But again, the COP is <i>huge</i>; I don't even want to think about how many successes would be needed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The COP has always been a bit of an odd duck in that regard. As the furthest out (another solar system) and the biggest (the size of a solar system) Horizon Realm it doesn't actually seem like a Horizon Realm at all, or at least not an Earth based one. Of course that far out size and distance may just be arbitrary qualities that an HR might have.<br /> <br /> The nature of the COP is heavily dependent on a number of metaphysical questions that are left up to the ST. The biggest is if Earth is the center of everything or just the center of a local area. The second biggest is if Earthy Foundations are universal or just, well, earthly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T05:09:06-07:00","id":1440009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1439972#post1439972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Void Ships are apparently able to maintain an Earth-like environment by tethering themselves to a Node on Earth apparently</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember correctly, this is a property all Horizon Realms had. Hence why ppl could live there w/o becoming spirits before the Storm. Void Adaptation isn't anything new, it was already in Book of Worlds with other name. In Infinite Tapestry its described how Realms lost their ties to Earth due to the Storm, and that's why they ceased protecting against it.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I would say it should work.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how the <i>size</i> of the realm factors in this, but maybe you would need several Nodes, perhaps too many. Powerful Realms had several Nodes attached to them<br /> <br /> Tied to that, from what I remember about the COP: I think most of the realm wasn't inhabited, by it's sheer size alone. I seem to remember the VE &quot;space colony&quot; was WAY large than they ever needed (let's remind that VE didn't built the COP, but rather found it), and thus they only inhabited a small portion of it<br /> <br /> One could chime in that maybe VE didn't use all of the Realm because it wasn't necessary AND because to &quot;void proof&quot; all of it would have required too many Nodes.<br /> <br /> Or say the Realm was an exception to the rules, as per <i>Ramnesis</i> - it was insinuated that the VE didn't built the old COP, but rather found the Realm in their explorations, after all. God and the ST knows what kind of powers worked over it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I had a thought about the VEs. I'm not sure if this is even plausible, but what they could really use to rebuild their numbers is to somehow make the COP a place where normal mortal humans can live and not become spirits. But I think I read somewhere that nobody born in &quot;space&quot; has Awakened, right? </div> </div> </div>I don't know about that.<br /> <br /> I don't see why Awakening in space should be impossible - though. It would be very unlikely simply because there wasn't a lot of ppl out there to begin with.<br /> <br /> Awakening requires a singular moment of truth, that wouldn't be any easier to get out there.<br /> <br /> Heck, perhaps it would be harder because sleepers could become accustomed to the odd, come to accept it as normal (I mean, Awakening it's misterious, but many Awakenings happen after traumatic, world changing, experiences - that's a tall order when Nephandi attacking inside flesh-ships it's what you call Monday)<br /> <br /> There are ways to &quot;teach&quot; Awakening but they're not certain to work (if they were super effective, mages wouldn't be so rare), and not any easier to implement out there than in Earth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even if it worked, how would they defend the COP? How did they ever defend it before? It's much bigger than Earth and has no Horizon. Whatever spells banished the Nephandi from Earth doesn't protect the COP either. </div> </div> </div>With crazy powerful magick. You either go big or go home, in the Deep Umbra<br /> <br /> And I would say the Technocracy can't quite go *that* big in it's current state. They should get a few more Archmasters before trying such a pharaonic approach to the Umbra problem ever again. Small, defensible, Realms are the way to go","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-15-2021, 08:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T05:28:46-07:00","id":1440010,"title":"","content":"<br /> As per general Realm defense. Realms have a few big advatages that make them very hard to invade by hostile forces, be them mages or spirits:<br /> <br /> *Reality it's defined by the mage who created the Realm, thus Paradox affects any invader that doesn't share the Paradigm.<br /> <br /> *It's not so easy to enter and leave Realms, for those that don't know how to do so.<br /> <br /> Any Realm it's surrounded by a Pericarp, that requires Spirit 5 to break by brute force, if I remember correctly. It's either that or entering trough a Portal built by the mages - Portals (and sometimes also the Pericarp, as was the case in Horizon) tend to be *very* well defended.<br /> <br /> So much so that Technocracy was unable to invade Horizon until a roge Hollow One ambassador betrayed the Traditions telling the Union of a back door (One of the many back doors built with less defenses that all Traditions had as a way to access and exit the Realm <i>unofficially </i>- Shady stuff, gotta love how mages so readily betray each other)<br /> <br /> If my understanding of the facts are correct (I didn't read Ascencion Warrior novels, only have second hand info from other books) Technocracy, with all their firepower, still were unable to just kick the front door. Too many deffenses built by too many Archmasters, I guess. Dirty betrayal doomed the Realm<br /> <br /> *Since the ppl who built the Realm define it's Reality and suffer no Paradox, there's no way to tell the powerful magicks they could have built inside it. In general mages would make the environment very hostile for those that don't know the rules of the Realm, and would have built quite a number of guardians and other defenses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-15-2021, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T09:29:19-07:00","id":1440054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So much so that Technocracy was unable to invade Horizon until a roge Hollow One ambassador betrayed the Traditions telling the Union of a back door (One of the many back doors built with less defenses that all Traditions had as a way to access and exit the Realm <i>unofficially </i>- Shady stuff, gotta love how mages so readily betray each other) </div> </div> </div>What a jackass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T13:18:06-07:00","id":1440095,"title":"","content":"As each known face of Threat Null reflects the original Convention books Technocracy taken to their final extreme, my headcanon on the absence of original Void Engineers reference, is that their exploratory wanderlust went to its final extreme and they \u201cboldly went\u201d off beyond the Deep Umbra never to return (yes I\u2019m aware that was their fate in Ascension as well, but I think it fits them going to their extreme - they lost touch with Earth delving into the deep beyond)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T13:38:42-07:00","id":1440100,"title":"","content":"The difference is that in Ascension, they presumably remained human. The Threat Null version involves them not just <i>consorting with</i> aliens, but <i>becoming</i> aliens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T13:41:03-07:00","id":1440101,"title":"","content":"Either way they'd become spirits, right?<br /> <br /> Also, weren't there a whole heap of Tradition Mages and Archmagi who became spirits, too? Wouldn't there be a lot of Etherites and Dreamspeakers in particular?<br /> <br /> Just because they become spirits, why would that mean they lose interest in the Ascension War, or lose interest in protecting Earth from Nephandi or whatever? I get the idea of ex-Void Engineers who just wander off and forget the Solar System, but the rest would stick around.<br /> <br /> Actually, it would be interesting to have some ex-VE and ex-Etherites who realize they're spirits now and don't have to worry about Magey politics, who have joined forces to fight Threat Null and the Nephandi, and explore the Solar System together.<br /> <br /> <br /> About the off-world HIT-Mark factories such as MECHA: are these controlled by the Autopolitans now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-15-2021, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T14:35:17-07:00","id":1440113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1440101#post1440101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either way they'd become spirits, right?<br /> <br /> Also, weren't there a whole heap of Tradition Mages and Archmagi who became spirits, too? Wouldn't there be a lot of Etherites and Dreamspeakers in particular?<br /> <br /> Just because they become spirits, why would that mean they lose interest in the Ascension War, or lose interest in protecting Earth from Nephandi or whatever? I get the idea of ex-Void Engineers who just wander off and forget the Solar System, but the rest would stick around.<br /> <br /> Actually, it would be interesting to have some ex-VE and ex-Etherites who realize they're spirits now and don't have to worry about Magey politics, who have joined forces to fight Threat Null and the Nephandi, and explore the Solar System together.<br /> <br /> <br /> About the off-world HIT-Mark factories such as MECHA: are these controlled by the Autopolitans now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bear in mind that when they become spirits, they cease to be mages: spirit powers replace Enlightenment/Arete and Spheres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T14:50:04-07:00","id":1440114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1440101#post1440101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either way they'd become spirits, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends, there are ways to avoid that.<br /> <br /> *Arguably batteries of Quint containing Earthly Ressonance could be used for a time.<br /> <br /> <br /> We don't know what's &quot;beyond the Deep Umbra&quot;, but the idea was to find another material world/s - no reason to think they will become Ephemera, if they can resist 'til they get there. Then again, they could end becoming very alien even w/o becoming spirits. They went very much outside any rulebook, at that point<br /> <br /> *High levels of DimSci (5?) allows one to protect against Void Adaptation.<br /> <br /> One of the theories about the fate of the VE it's that they never suffered from Void Adaptation OR that they actually Void Adapted on their own terms. The book says something across the lines off: &quot;If someone knew about Void Adaptation, it would be the VE Masters&quot;...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, weren't there a whole heap of Tradition Mages and Archmagi who became spirits, too? Wouldn't there be a lot of Etherites and Dreamspeakers in particular?<br /> <br /> Just because they become spirits, why would that mean they lose interest in the Ascension War, or lose interest in protecting Earth from Nephandi or whatever? I get the idea of ex-Void Engineers who just wander off and forget the Solar System, but the rest would stick around. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there are. Altrough many also just died on the Storm (and the Horizon War)<br /> <br /> There has been speculation on the fandom about a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/533448-threat-null-where-will-it-be-covered\">Traditional version of Threat Null</a><br /> <br /> However, The Word of God it's that the spirits left by Taditional mages are more like individuals trapped on their own projects and rutine. They're like Wraith Drones, they have no agency, instead just going trough the motions.<br /> <br /> They're not seen as a power that could help, as much as a sad fate to be avoided.<br /> <br /> But, let's keep this in mind:<br /> <br /> The book that talks about Traditional mages turning to spirit, Infinite Tappestry, it's arround 20+ years older than the book that talks about Threath Null. I think that, more than likely, the goal-posts changed a LOT between these books. <hr />See:<br /> <br /> Infinite Tappestry was the book about the Umbra in an edition that had been very much <i>against</i> going to the Umbra since it started.<br /> <br /> Before that book, the big no-no about playing in the Umbra was the Avatar Storm inflicting damage and potentially Gilguling your character (that caused, perhaps, the biggest war in Mage fandom ever. The backlash was so huge it get's mentioned in some sourcebooks - from the pov of the authors, of course)<br /> <br /> Now, in the midst of this conflict - with ppl saying entering the Umbra was too punishing - comes Infinite Tapestry: A book about getting into the Umbra.<br /> <br /> This book offers THE largest compendium of ways to avoid the Storm. And not only trough rare Merits or rare locations: From mid to hard difficulty Rotes that avoid it entirely, to one sensory effect (I think it was Spirit 1/Entropy 1 - but I don't remember) that allows to find weak spots in the Storm in order to take less damage, you have many ways to protect against it. Hence the Storm it's no longer such a big problem, you don't need to be &quot;super special&quot; anymore to get trough more or less safely<br /> <br /> But that book it's still very much a product of Revised Philosophy: It just changes the goalposts - it gives a lot of options to bypass the Storm, but it focuses instead on something that was already in Book of Worlds but never was a big deal before: Disembodiment - what VE call Void Adaptation<br /> <br /> That wasn't such a big deal back then because being in a Realm avoided the effect. I'm not 100% sure, but perhaps Infinite Tappestry it's the book where Earthly Ressonance get's introduced as the reason why. In any case, it's stated that the Storm cut the threads that made Realms &quot;connect&quot; with Earth, thus erasing their protective effect on those who inhabited them.<br /> <br /> Clearly the intention was that becoming a spirit isn't cool, it's a pathetic fate you want to avoid at all costs. It's the Wassail from Vampire...it's a way to have adventures in the Umbra while at the same time making sure these take less than three months - thus Mages can't just go away and live there.<br /> <br /> Threath Null, on the other hand, was introduced as antagonists. So they had to be more active...<br /> <br /> Now, it's said that Treath Null it's so cohesive because it has Conditioning as part of their making. But that <i>by itself </i>doesn't explain why they aren't mostly harmless drones doing whatever they were doing before converting, like Traditionalists seem to be...being &quot;on the same page&quot; doesn't mean the page it's going to be particularly interesting. One needs agency.<br /> <br /> <i>A simple explanation could be that powers with more agency (VE that were able to make themselves inmune to the effect, the Computer, etc. Who knows?) are directing them.</i> <hr /><br /> Frankly, while I can see Traditional spirits being every bit as alien, and nowhere near AS cohesive as Treath Null...<br /> <br /> I also think that them having no agency, and pululating the same dusty Realms repeating tasks may be dramatic, but it's also kinda boring. The product of an Era that wanted Mages out of the Umbra, out of the War, doing &quot;street level&quot; jobs and stuff...I would rather embrace the ideas for a Traditional Threat Null than say Traditional spirits are incapable of doing anything","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-15-2021, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T15:29:02-07:00","id":1440118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1440101#post1440101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either way they'd become spirits, right?<br /> <br /> Also, weren't there a whole heap of Tradition Mages and Archmagi who became spirits, too? Wouldn't there be a lot of Etherites and Dreamspeakers in particular?<br /> <br /> Just because they become spirits, why would that mean they lose interest in the Ascension War, or lose interest in protecting Earth from Nephandi or whatever? I get the idea of ex-Void Engineers who just wander off and forget the Solar System, but the rest would stick around.<br /> <br /> Actually, it would be interesting to have some ex-VE and ex-Etherites who realize they're spirits now and don't have to worry about Magey politics, who have joined forces to fight Threat Null and the Nephandi, and explore the Solar System together.<br /> <br /> <br /> About the off-world HIT-Mark factories such as MECHA: are these controlled by the Autopolitans now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits don\u2019t think like humans. They\u2019re concepts, archetypes, not people. Hence the rest of Threat Null becoming exaggerated horror versions of their Conventions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T15:37:28-07:00","id":1440120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1440114#post1440114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There has been speculation on the fandom about a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/533448-threat-null-where-will-it-be-covered\">Traditional version of Threat Null</a><br /> <br /> However, The Word of God it's that the spirits left by Taditional mages are more like individuals trapped on their own projects and rutine. They're like Wraith Drones, they have no agency, instead just going trough the motions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m slightly annoyed that my Tradition Threat Null equivalents were quoted without me being credited on that thread, but whatever.<br /> <br /> So the Word of God was that the Traditions\u2019 pluralism meaning they\u2019re not the equivalents of Old School Technocracy means they wouldn\u2019t become the same thing. Listening to some interviews with Satyros recently though I increasingly am reaffirmed in my disagreement with this argument. The previous editions were making a big point of the failings of the Old Masters before the Avatar Storm. How they were too hidebound and solipsistic, escaping into their personal paradigm bubbles rather than working together across paradigmatic lines as should be the point of the Nine Traditions. That being the case SOME turning into Threat Null equivalents as dangerous embodiments of paradigm makes sense to me. They aren\u2019t united like Threat Null, since Control was not part of their paradigm, and probably fighting each other most of the time reduces their threat to Earth, but I definitely still have them out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T15:48:46-07:00","id":1440122,"title":"","content":"A lot of the 500-year-old archmasters who dislike everyone outside of their Tradition would become very unpleasant, sure. They were already rather unpleasant. But weren't there also younger Mages in the Umbra, especially from the Sons of Ether and the Dreamspeakers?<br /> <br /> Anyway, the idea that anyone who was sapient, becoming a spirit and suddenly having less intelligence and agency than the least of gafflings, is just wrongheaded to me. They should become free-willed spirits who remember being human. And perhaps regret that as spirits they're not as powerful as when they were mages. But still sapient beings, not vegetables. Literal vegetables (and rocks) in the Umbra have more agency and intelligence than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T16:15:44-07:00","id":1440124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1440122#post1440122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of the 500-year-old archmasters who dislike everyone outside of their Tradition would become very unpleasant, sure. They were already rather unpleasant. But weren't there also younger Mages in the Umbra, especially from the Sons of Ether and the Dreamspeakers?<br /> <br /> Anyway, the idea that anyone who was sapient, becoming a spirit and suddenly having less intelligence and agency than the least of gafflings, is just wrongheaded to me. They should become free-willed spirits who remember being human. And perhaps regret that as spirits they're not as powerful as when they were mages. But still sapient beings, not vegetables. Literal vegetables (and rocks) in the Umbra have more agency and intelligence than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, as I said not all Tradition Mages would become Threat Null equivalents, just said they\u2019d exist too.<br /> <br /> I think you are wrong about what spirits are. The idea that a spirit is going to act like a person is wrongheaded to me. It\u2019s not a question of free will, it\u2019s a question of what their desires and ideas to act on are, not their ability to act. They\u2019re not people. They\u2019re ideas. Archetypes that express a theme or concept. All spirits are including those rock and vegetable spirits you mentioned. If they were just the same person now with default ephemeral body, but otherwise themselves unchanged, it would defeat the entire point of the threat of discorporeation/void adaptation. Humans that turn into spirits are spirits, and behave accordingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T16:38:57-07:00","id":1440125,"title":"","content":"As glamourweaver pointed out earlier, Void Adaptation was a thing before the Dimensional Anomaly. So was Conditioning. But Threat Null was not. I've come to the conclusion that there's one more ingredient needed to get a Threat Null phenomenon: Control. Specifically, Control's response to being cut off from Earth. Threat Null wasn't the natural result of Conditioned Technocrats undergoing Void Adaptation, though those are necessary elements of Threat Null. No, it was <i>engineered by Control</i>, as a way to build an army in the Umbra to help retake Earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T17:37:26-07:00","id":1440131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1440118#post1440118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spirits don\u2019t think like humans. They\u2019re concepts, archetypes, not people. Hence the rest of Threat Null becoming exaggerated horror versions of their Conventions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I don't think they're not mindless.<br /> <br /> No, they're so much worse than mindless.<br /> <br /> They are <b>perfected</b>.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/38/Cyberman_2020_redesign.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T01:48:22-07:00","id":1440166,"title":"","content":"The Cyberman is a good choice. The man who created them was a self described alchemist. They were meant to be humans who had gained a form of Enlightenment but paid a terrible price for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T05:00:46-07:00","id":1440183,"title":"","content":"The Borg are another example: Transhumanity (the Progenitors counterpart in Threat Null) even exhibits a similar hive mind \u2014 though in that regard, they're more like Gaia from Isaac Asimov's later Foundation novels (<i>Foundation's Edge</i> and <i>Foundation and Earth</i>).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T08:09:34-07:00","id":1440201,"title":"","content":"I don't recognize or understand those sci-fi references, except the Borg. I do not agree that Mages who become spirits should all be like the Borg or like the drones in Wraith. When I played Orpheus, the drone we had to deal with was mindless. He pantomimed the same motions over and over again, unaware of his surroundings. He typed on a computer that was off. He couldn't see or hear us when were were right there next to him. He was utterly mindless in a way that spirits simply aren't.<br /> <br /> Spirits don't think like humans but they are <b>people</b>, not punch-card computers or undead drones. They have sentient, sapient minds and free will and agency. For gafflings, their goals and interests are exceedingly narrow, but they still have emotions and sensation of their surroundings, and are capable of conversation. Jagglings have full individuality and personality and broader interests, and are a much better analogy for what happens when a sapient individual human (or shapeshifter) becomes a spirit. Certainly when a shapeshifter becomes an ancestor spirit or a Greater Uktena, there's no indication that this is a terrible awful thing that strips away their mind, personality, individuality, sapience, and/or sentience. Even when humans become Wratihs, which are clearly messed up beings, they don't all become drones. Bargaining with a spirit is not like programming a computer, precisely because spirits are not mindless machines.<br /> <br /> Incarnae are very complicated individuals, but I don't think a Mage should have a chance to become an Incarna unless they were already a high-Arete Archmaster or an Exemplar.<br /> <br /> The thing is that becoming a spirit is like becoming an Exemplar, but more so: you lose all Dynamic Magick and the ability to gain more enlightenment, let alone Ascend. You can't even reincarnate to try again. Whatever you are is all you'll ever be, because you don't even really embody a concept that exists in the material world so there's nothing driving you to grow and change in an animist way.<br /> <br /> I don't think that every Mage who becomes a spirit should become as messed up as the Threat Null or the Borg. They are, like you said, the result of something unusually deranged and malevolent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-16-2021, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T09:34:59-07:00","id":1440212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1440201#post1440201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> When I played Orpheus, the drone we had to deal with was mindless. He pantomimed the same motions over and over again, unaware of his surroundings. He typed on a computer that was off. He couldn't see or hear us when were were right there next to him. He was utterly mindless in a way that spirits simply aren't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps I exaggerated. But only a little. Even in Infinite tappestry you can <i>talk </i>with a spirit mage<br /> <br /> But the spirit of a Master would have difficulty to recognize its own pupil, and won't accept to acknowledge changes on himself or the world around.<br /> <br /> An example: Victoria Station (Etherite Realm) spirits are described as &quot;reenacting the events of previous eras like clockwork&quot;, and that they believe they're in the Victorian Era. But it's also said that they have heard Technocracy won the Ascencion War (it's Revised ppl), but refuse to believe it - which already means they can hear stuff. The way it's talked the spirits would never leave their Realms.<br /> <br /> A concrete example: Proffesor Dubrius walks the corridors directing spirit consors and Acolites to errands. Claims that can leave the Realm wheneve he wants, but doesn't want to (implying that he can't). You could ask him to repair some stuff and consult about various destinations across the Horizon, but much of it's information it's outdated (implying he can't or won't actualize).<br /> <br /> Perhaps gafflings would be a good example of that kind of attitude: cuasi-mechanical, almost unaware, but aware enough to talk and help with some basic stuff under purview.<br /> <br /> I do think Jagglings would be a more entertaining fate to have them as potential allies/antagonists, instead of prop for a Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-16-2021, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T09:56:15-07:00","id":1440215,"title":"","content":"<br /> Clearly Threat Null ain't like Victoria Station &quot;ghosts&quot; - but not because they &quot;work together thanks to Conditioning&quot;, rather because they can clearly leave/enter their Realms. They react in smarter ways and have agendas with the outside world - because otherwise they would hardly be much of an antagonist faction.<br /> <br /> The only similarity it's that they believe to be the <i>real</i> Technocracy, and that earthers have gone Roge. So you can see some disconnection (but one that acknowledges a change in the outside world - earthers being roge)<br /> <br /> This isn't really a contradiction. It would make sense if they're being controlled, which it's hinted everywhere. By Control, the Computer or some other entity that has a greater degree of sapience. Heck, Control caling earthers &quot;rogue&quot; would make a lot of sense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T10:02:29-07:00","id":1440216,"title":"","content":"For all we know, the Computer is the Authochthonian aspect of Control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T12:46:48-07:00","id":1440235,"title":"","content":"The thing about Threat Null is that they are Technocrats who were ALREADY brainwashed by their own people into being completely loyal to their Paradigm and hating all non-Technocratic Paradigms. Threat Null shouldn't necessarily be mindless but they should all be 100% loyal to the cause of destroying all beliefs but a perfect sterile Union society.<br /> <br /> On a scale of 1-10 of old Conditioning levels.<br /> <br /> Conditioning 11.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T13:01:45-07:00","id":1440239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1440212#post1440212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps I exaggerated. But only a little. Even in Infinite tappestry you can <i>talk </i>with a spirit mage<br /> <br /> But the spirit of a Master would have difficulty to recognize its own pupil, and won't accept to acknowledge changes on himself or the world around.<br /> <br /> An example: Victoria Station (Etherite Realm) spirits are described as &quot;reenacting the events of previous eras like clockwork&quot;, and that they believe they're in the Victorian Era. But it's also said that they have heard Technocracy won the Ascencion War (it's Revised ppl), but refuse to believe it - which already means they can hear stuff. The way it's talked the spirits would never leave their Realms.<br /> <br /> A concrete example: Proffesor Dubrius walks the corridors directing spirit consors and Acolites to errands. Claims that can leave the Realm wheneve he wants, but doesn't want to (implying that he can't). You could ask him to repair some stuff and consult about various destinations across the Horizon, but much of it's information it's outdated (implying he can't or won't actualize).<br /> <br /> Perhaps gafflings would be a good example of that kind of attitude: cuasi-mechanical, almost unaware, but aware enough to talk and help with some basic stuff under purview.<br /> <br /> I do think Jagglings would be a more entertaining fate to have them as potential allies/antagonists, instead of prop for a Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I think that's a terrible way to write them. But a lot about Revised was terrible IMO. What you describe is barely an emanation, let alone a gaffling. It's just a drone that can parrot-talk, a RL robot with a handful of programmed responses. Some emanations are nothing more than that, but some have more awareness, memories, free will, and even capacity to learn than that - just see Dystopia's population. Gafflings are not trapped in any realm and are more aware and able to learn and change than emanations. Normally large changes to a Gaffling are put on them from an external source, but they aren't just videos playing on a 3D screen.<br /> <br /> Mages should become jaggling spirits, not sub-emanation semi-drones. They should not be stripped of all memories or personality, or be imprisoned in any Realm. It doesn't even make any sense for them to become emanations - I could see Sleepers becoming emanations, but even an Apprentice Mage should become a gaffling. Especially since Revised had every Horizon Realm completely and utterly cease to exist, all those emanations/drones would cease to exist too.<br /> <br /> Becoming a Wraith is a pretty crappy fate that nobody wants, and that isn't accomplished by make every wraith a mindless drone, or stripping away all memories and making them all just identical.<br /> <br /> If a Mage becomes a spirit they:<br /> 1. Can never return to Earth.<br /> 2. Lose all Awakened Magick, forever.<br /> 3. Can never increase Arete, Ascend, or even reincarnate.<br /> 4. Can no longer reproduce.<br /> 5. Can no longer think like a human being, or expand their understanding or mind beyond what it was before.<br /> 6. Probably can't become a spirit familiar either.<br /> 7. Probably can't teach an apprentice, even under the best circumstance.<br /> 8. Are cut off from nearly everyone on Earth.<br /> <br /> The above is already very sucky and unattractive, not to mention unplayable with in any normal game, without replacing them with mindless robot clones with no memories of any part of their human life, and even less ability to form memories than the protagonist in <i>Memento</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-16-2021, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T13:03:27-07:00","id":1440240,"title":"","content":"And more and more, I'm coming to the conclusion that there shouldn't be a void engineer counterpart among Threat Null. They never had the conditioning. That's not to say that there aren't any former void engineers that have undergone void adaptation: there are plenty. But they're just your ordinary, run-of-the-mill Void-Adapted Scientists, with none of the stuff that makes Threat Null what it is. No different, in that respect, from mages turned spirits, save only for the fact that their innate wanderlust means that they're unlikely to be bound to a specific Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T13:18:28-07:00","id":1440244,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I don't think that Threat Null should be alien at all.<br /> <br /> Just make them like the Seers of the Throne.<br /> <br /> They're all in the service of corrupt Weaver/Cyber Gods and only free from Conditioning do the other Technocrats realize this is insane and treason against Humanity.<br /> <br /> You could also have other Technocrats WILLINGLY JOIN because they offer power and wealth or a promise to destroy their enemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T13:23:56-07:00","id":1440249,"title":"","content":"Arg, I spent too long editing my post and didn't realize you had already responded.<br /> Edit: Well, Dataweaver posted almost at the same minute I did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-16-2021, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T13:57:33-07:00","id":1440257,"title":"","content":"Again, Threat Null was conceived in the context of the Avatar Storm. As presented, it represents the Technocracy in the Umbra. That's a big part of why the roster of Threat Null consists of Technocrats who have undergone Void Adaptation and are no longer human. <br /> <br /> I also tend to think that the \u201cno longer human\u201d thing is particularly appropriate to the Autochthonians and Transhumanity, as they're representative of Iteration X's and the Progenitors' respective desires to go beyond the limits of humanity. The Agents and Residents don't quitefeel as compelling to me, largely because the NWO and the Syndicate are not about moving beyond humanity.<br /> <br /> What you're describing, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a>, is what I would call a \u201cThreat Null victory\u201d scenario: it's what you get when and if Threat Null succeeds in its goal of invading Earth and retaking control of the Technocratic Union. And in games where I want the Union to be unmistakably the bad guys, it would definitely be an avenue to consider pursuing. I might even consider replacing the notion of Nephandic infiltration with this as a rationale behind the Union deciding to reorganize and purge itself of the various reformist elements in it. <br /> <br /> But I wouldn't want it presented as the default status of the Technocracy. I <i>like</i> the fact that M20 doesn't try to force one approach down your throat, and that the Technocracy doesn't <i>have</i> to be the unambiguous bad guys. (Although in that regard, my own personal preference is to go ahead and split Navalon off from the Union, and have <i>it</i> represent Enlightened Science that's comparatively free of corruption, while still being sciency enough to appeal to those who dismiss the Etherites as quacks and the VAs as cyber-mystics.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T14:05:50-07:00","id":1440259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1440257#post1440257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, Threat Null was conceived in the context of the Avatar Storm. As presented, it represents the Technocracy in the Umbra. That's a big part of why the roster of Threat Null consists of Technocrats who have undergone Void Adaptation and are no longer human.<br /> <br /> I also tend to think that the \u201cno longer human\u201d thing is particularly appropriate to the Autochthonians and Transhumanity, as they're representative of Iteration X's and the Progenitors' respective desires to go beyond the limits of humanity. The Agents and Residents don't quitefeel as compelling to me, largely because the NWO and the Syndicate are not about moving beyond humanity.<br /> <br /> What you're describing, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a>, is what I would call a \u201cThreat Null victory\u201d scenario: it's what you get when and if Threat Null succeeds in its goal of invading Earth and retaking control of the Technocratic Union. And in games where I want the Union to be unmistakably the bad guys, it would definitely be an avenue to consider pursuing. I might even consider replacing the notion of Nephandic infiltration with this as a rationale behind the Union deciding to reorganize and purge itself of the various reformist elements in it.<br /> <br /> But I wouldn't want it presented as the default status of the Technocracy. I <i>like</i> the fact that M20 doesn't try to force one approach down your throat, and that the Technocracy doesn't <i>have</i> to be the unambiguous bad guys. (Although in that regard, my own personal preference is to go ahead and split Navalon off from the Union, and have <i>it</i> represent Enlightened Science that's comparatively free of corruption, while still being sciency enough to appeal to those who dismiss the Etherites as quacks and the VAs as cyber-mystics.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly, I don't think that would be a very interesting game.<br /> <br /> I think a much more interesting game would be Threat Null operating on Earth and the Technocracy versus them. Threat Null in the Umbra is....well, lame. Imagine however, the Syndicate versus Syndicate Plus. You never see the Technocracy actually USE its vast mortal influence and wealth in battles against the Traditions but against something like Threat Null you could have all manner of fascinating and awesome contests of money, power, brainwashing, propaagnda, and more.<br /> <br /> I think definitely Threat Null needs to invade Earth and establish a beach head. I also am hoping the &quot;regular&quot; Union can avoid being brainwashed in such an event.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T14:31:08-07:00","id":1440272,"title":"","content":"Threat Null was originally conceived of as an enemy for the Void Engineers in particular. In the Revised Convention Books, it was the dirty secret that the VEs we're hiding from the rest of the Union, because they knew that the other conventions wouldn't understand the danger, and would get gobbled up by Threat Null. That's why Threat Null has the ability to co-opt Technocrats who are subject to Conditioning, and why the VEs are trying so desperately to keep them off of Earth \u2014 up to and including deploying a satellite network designed to artificially strengthen the Avatar Storm, as that's helping to keep Threat 6 at bay. <br /> <br /> And if Threat Null ever does get through to Earth, they won't compete with the Union; they'll assimilate it. Which will leave the VEs in a very awkward position.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T17:01:49-07:00","id":1440296,"title":"","content":"If they're spirits, it isn't simple for them to return to the material world, Avatar Storm or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T21:19:50-07:00","id":1440323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1440296#post1440296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they're spirits, it isn't simple for them to return to the material world, Avatar Storm or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>In an updated campaign, I'd assume they'd start recruiting Technocratic Agents on the Material World and have them summon them into bodies via SCIENCE.<br /> <br /> You know, like the Gould or data uploads vis cybernetics.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T10:48:57-07:00","id":1440364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1440124#post1440124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, as I said not all Tradition Mages would become Threat Null equivalents, just said they\u2019d exist too.<br /> <br /> I think you are wrong about what spirits are. The idea that a spirit is going to act like a person is wrongheaded to me. It\u2019s not a question of free will, it\u2019s a question of what their desires and ideas to act on are, not their ability to act. They\u2019re not people. They\u2019re ideas. Archetypes that express a theme or concept. All spirits are including those rock and vegetable spirits you mentioned. If they were just the same person now with default ephemeral body, but otherwise themselves unchanged, it would defeat the entire point of the threat of discorporeation/void adaptation. Humans that turn into spirits are spirits, and behave accordingly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We have a reasonably good baseline of what a human turned spirit is in the form of Wraiths, and they both do and don't act like the original person. They have all the memories of the original but if we presume that the Passions system is supposed to be representative of what is actually going on then specific strong memories and emotions are much more important to them than the rest. Indeed it is very possible for their emotions and bonds to become more important to them than the reason for those emotions and bonds. It can be difficult to tell if they are the original person or the spirit of the memory of that person.<br /> <br /> For the record I consider them to be the real person (at least partly), but it is difficult to see how they would act differently if they were just memory spirits.<br /> <br /> I would portray the discorporated similarly. They are still the Mage, but they are heavily inclined to see the world through the lens of the idea or legend of that Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T13:43:06-07:00","id":1440382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1440364#post1440364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> We have a reasonably good baseline of what a human turned spirit is in the form of Wraiths, and they both do and don't act like the original person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not remotely the same thing and pretending otherwise is disingenuous. Umbrood of the High, Middle, and Deep Umbra are nothing like Wraiths in behavior or mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T13:47:23-07:00","id":1440383,"title":"","content":"Umbrood are native to the Umbra and are not in any way formerly human. And yet real spirits and wraiths both have personhood. Emanations, which have no personhood, are just 3E video loops made out of moving ephemera, and are projections of a Realm rather than living creatures. There's no reason for mages to lose their personhood and become mindless 3D video loops when they become spirits.<br /> <br /> It's absurd that Infinite Tapestry made disconnected Mages have drastically less mental capacity than any wraith <b>or</b> Umbral spirit, let alone zero capacity to form new memories. It's also nonsensical to make them emanations native to a specific realm, when they <b>aren't</b> native and those realms have all been utterly destroyed.<br /> <br /> I could believe a mere sleeper becoming an emanation if they spent their whole disconnection time in one particular realm. But even an apprentice mage should become a gaffling at least, and any other mage should become a jaggling. Their souls are too strong to be utterly 100% erased like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-17-2021, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T23:43:47-07:00","id":1440414,"title":"","content":"I think the description in Book Of Barriers gives a good indication of their mindset:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Explorers without shapeshifter blood eventually lose<br /> their connection to the Earth if they stay in the Umbra for<br /> long. After a while (<b>one to four months for most people,<br /> four months to a year for primal mysticks</b>), they forget their<br /> lives on Earth and become spirits. Their physical bodies<br /> fall away (or die, in the case of astral travelers) and <b>their<br /> consciousness shifts them into spirits which embody their<br /> true nature</b>. This is a one-way process. Umbrood like Aelida<br /> are said to have begun their existence as mortals who fled<br /> the material plane. </div> </div> </div>Note that in case a plot is post-avatar-storm or avatar-storm-has-not-happened, I'd again go for the much longer disconnection period for the primals (Dreamspeakers, Verbena, etc.), instead of the 3-months-for-everybody described in Infinite Tapestry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 03-19-2021, 02:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T05:15:09-07:00","id":1440447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1440382#post1440382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not remotely the same thing and pretending otherwise is disingenuous. Umbrood of the High, Middle, and Deep Umbra are nothing like Wraiths in behavior or mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's not disingenuous in the slightest. Your standard Umbrood has never been human, doesn't have human memories, and doesn't have human-adjacent motivations. A discorporated Mage has, has, and may. In that sense he is much more similar to a Wraith than to an Umbrood. I am not suggesting we use Wraith mechanics for anything other than Wraiths. Instead I am looking at what those mechanics are trying to simulate and how that might apply to humans-turned-spirits. <br /> <br /> \u200bEven if we presume that void adaptation works by instantly replacing the Mage with a standard spirit that spirit will still be intimately connected to the identity of the Mage. It is a spirit, yes, but its desires and purviews are not esoteric concepts. It would be like replacing the Mage with the image he presents in his autobiography or his self image, but giving that image all or some of his memories. <br /> <br /> Or not. We could just assume that the Mages lose everything that made them what they are, but given that Threat Null has a connection to the ideas of the Conventions they came from, that's not the way I would take it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T08:11:32-07:00","id":1440455,"title":"","content":"Who counts as primal mysticks, besides Dreamspeakers and Verbenae?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T08:43:10-07:00","id":1440457,"title":"","content":"In M20 terms, it would have to be a Focus thing. Anyone with a Focus similar enough to the Dreamspeakers or Verbenae ought to qualify.<br /> <br /> Though frankly, that whole notion makes me feel uncomfortable.in particular, I don't like the idea of such a significant advantage when it comes to the Umbra being handed out \u201cfor free\u201d, as it were. Either there should be some sort of downside or mixed blessing associated with it, or it should be something like a Merit or Background that those with appropriate Foci are eligible to take.<br /> <br /> And then there's the notion that the void engineers don't get anything like it. If any technomancers should be able to get that sort of a benefit, it should be the void engineers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T10:05:16-07:00","id":1440462,"title":"","content":"In Infinite Tappestry, one of the ways to get protection against Void Adaptation was trough the Totem Background.<br /> <br /> Back then it worked differently, more like how it works in Werewolf, and one of the things you could buy was a degree of inmunity to that effect - albeit it had the price of taking some characteristics of the personality and the body of the Totem.<br /> <br /> This idea of protecting oneself by actually (but temporarily) <i>embracing</i> the spirit form as a protection reminds me also of the VE Rote, LERMUization (I think it was called something like that, you know, the Rote where you become a &quot;gray&quot; alien). <hr /><br /> I think one could adapt the first idea to M20 saying the Totem Background allows for an easier version of VE Rote. And perhaps one could recover the old rule of &quot;one year and a day&quot; saying that's using that Rote allows one to suspend the Void Adaptation that much time, as you gain some control of the transformation.<br /> <br /> That way VE have it, and primal mages have easier access to it trough having a Totem","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T10:59:59-07:00","id":1440469,"title":"","content":"And another possibility would be to add that to the list of benefits that a Familiar can grant. The Dreamspeakers, in this view of things, don't have a longer staying power in the Umbra because of their focus, but because they tend to have the Totem Background; and the Verbenae get <i>their</i> extra staying power by virtue of being the Tradition Most Likely To Have A Familiar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T11:16:16-07:00","id":1440473,"title":"","content":"The Totem background Sparks an idea. Have the Spirit of Exploration appear to VEs and Trad mages cut off from Earth by the reality storm. He allows them to take him (he's in the form of James T. Kirk ) as a totem. He takes these mages and a large group of space settlers and chantry dwellers to settle on an Earthlike world in deep space. <br /> <br /> The Spirit of Exploration wants enough of the Mages and consors to see this planet as home and a place they won't leave. Then the Spirit will allow contact to be re-established. The whole planet full of humans ploy is about bringing back exploration as a present day reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T12:01:33-07:00","id":1440482,"title":"","content":"Getting back to the original subject of the thread: in my head-canon, the spatial horizon is in effect the boundary of the solar system. The Solar System isn't the center of the universe, with the Deep Universe being all that's beyond it; rather, the Deep Universe contains a multitude of worlds, each similar to Earth with a surrounding \u201cConventional Space\u201d separated from the Umbra by a Gauntlet. The worlds within these pockets of \u201cnormalcy\u201d don't have the same base reality that we do, so when we visit them we are the aliens. However, they are not part of the Void, and visitors to these worlds do not need to fear Void Adaptation while they are there. Instead, they have to contend with hostile Environmental Conditions, which I borrow from the STV supplement <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/product/314491\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Countless Dreams</a> (pp.27\u201333)*. This gives an option where old style VEs can do the Star Trek thing, exploring strange new worlds, seeking out new life and new civilizations, and boldly going where no human has gone before; meanwhile, new style void engineers can do the Avatar thing, where they find a Pandora like world and set out to plunder its native resources. Or at least, that's what they might do if they had the time and energy to do more than just be the last line of defense for Earth. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the actual aliens out there aren't really Umbrood; the ones that we've encountered who <i>are</i> are actually Void Adapted aliens.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> * For what it's worth, I highly recommend <b>Countless Dreams</b>, for both Changeling and Mage games with heavy sci-fi/space opera elements. It needs some tweaking to work without changeling, and probably could use some tweaking if you aren't interested in its specific premise (that the Countless are alien refugees in Earth who have fused themselves with human hosts to survive after a catastrophe wiped out their homeworlds); but there are a lot of useful ideas and game systems to borrow for exotic aliens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-18-2021, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T14:25:23-07:00","id":1440497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1440457#post1440457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In M20 terms, it would have to be a Focus thing. Anyone with a Focus similar enough to the Dreamspeakers or Verbenae ought to qualify.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, but at the time it was written who did it refer to?<br /> <br /> <br /> As for being a free benefit, all Technocrats (including Void Engineers) get the free benefit of <s>ruling the world</s> enormous political and economic and cultural power, and magic that rarely attracts Paradox or negative attention. Don't they also get gobs of money real easy, and an entire Background for access to cyborg armies? Do mysticks get anything to compensate/balance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-18-2021, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T14:39:26-07:00","id":1440499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1440497#post1440497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, but at the time it was written who did it refer to?</div> </div> </div> </div> prior to M20, the game had a massive bias toward the Traditions, to the extent that witchcraft and Verbena were treated essentially as synonyms, for example. As such, when they said primal mages such as Verbenae or Dreamspeakers, they pretty much meant Verbenae or Dreamspeakers; and if you pushed the point, they'd probably allow that the rare non-Verbena witch or non-Dreamspeaker shaman would also count. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1440497#post1440497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for being a free benefit, all Technocrats (including Void Engineers) get the free benefit of ruling the world, and magic that rarely attracts Paradox or negative attention. Don't they also get gobs of money real easy? They don't appear balanced with mysticks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's just agree to disagree on this; I really don't want to go down the rabbit-hole of being accused of \u201cwhite room game balance\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T15:04:30-07:00","id":1440501,"title":"","content":"I phrased it badly. I'm not really disagreeing, more like wondering, since I haven't read any corebook yet (I did finally buy one).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-18-2021, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T17:09:47-07:00","id":1440511,"title":"","content":"That's okay. For what it's worth, I misspoke too. Let me try it again\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026but in a new thread; because, well, you'll see once I've posted it. (And I'll edit in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra\">a link to it</a> here once I do.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-18-2021, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T21:10:59-07:00","id":1440537,"title":"","content":"Ported back over from the other thread: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440513-reality-zones-and-the-umbra?p=1440531#post1440531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the reason I challenged you was my question about game balance: is it a bad thing if mysticks get some unique advantages? Aren't Technocrats automatically <i>strongly</i> advantaged by the setting? They sure look like they are, but I'm asking if my impression is correct. I also usually root for the underdogs and dangit, the Technos are the ones who created the Avatar Storm. On purpose! So part of me just says they deserve to get burned by it. Not that there is anything resembling cosmic justice or fair karma in the WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Technocracy did <i>not</i> create the Avatar Storm on purpose. They were involved in the series of events that lead to the Avatar Storm, such as frying an Antediluvian and setting off a nuke in the Underworld; but the latter was the action of a rogue VE, not something sanctioned by the Technocracy. And it triggered the Sixth Great Maelstrom in the Underworld, which certainly wasn't the Technocracy's intent; but don't conflate the Sixth Great Maelstrom with the Avatar Storm: the Avatar Storm kicked in a little bit after the 6GM arose, but it was a separate phenomenon. <br /> <br /> Likewise, the attack on the Ravnos Antediluvian wasn't done to trigger the Avatar Storm; it was done because an incredibly powerful monster was rampaging across India and was causing tremendous harm, and needed to be stopped. <br /> <br /> The Avatar Storm has been described by some as a massive Paradox Backlash. Nobody intended for it to happen. The Void Engineers, in particular, were devastated by it, precisely because they didn't see it coming until it hit them. <br /> <br /> And the reason why the Technocracy has a powerful advantage in the modern setting is because it <i>worked</i> for it. Not in nice ways, granted; but they put in the effort. It didn't just <i>happen</i>. Even with my pet theory that Technocratic Reality is built on the Earthly Foundations and thus is easier to get buy-in from the Consensus than other Reality Zones are, there was never anything <i>inevitable</i> about Technocratic Reality Zone dominance. <br /> <br /> Conversely, I wasn't complaining about the Union somehow being disadvantaged by the way the Umbra works (except the Void Engineers; but that's a separate issue in my mind); my main complaint in this regard was that only shamans and witches were getting the extended survival, which in turn carries implications about the nature of the Umbra which I've addressed in the other thread. I'm not thinking in terms of what would be just; barring the discovery of the Sphere of Telos (see the Time of Judgement book <b>Ascension</b>), there's no guarantee of justice in the World of Darkness. And whether or not there <i>can</i> or <i>will</i> be justice is one of those things that's a hotly contested point in the Ascension War: there are whole Paradigms (in the M20 sense of the term) devoted to that question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-19-2021, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T09:40:34-07:00","id":1440610,"title":"","content":"I am talking about the Avatar Storm, not the Sixth Great Maelstrom. The Storm was caused by regular non-Nephandi VEs dropping a spirit nuke (not a normal nuke) on Bangladesh. I'm skeptical that a soul-nuke designed to obliterate entire layers of the Umbra &quot;accidentally&quot; did precisely that. Why would they not use a weapon designed to affect the material world, where Zapathasura actually was located? It's not plausible that they had no normal tactical nukes. Certainly they didn't expect it to hurt them, but they did design a weapon to destroy the Umbra.<br /> <br /> But my question about the advantage of Technocrats was also about game balance. If the PC options aren't balanced, that's a problem with the game. You're not trying to say they are balanced. I'm not sure what you're saying to justify it but it isn't relevant to my concern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T10:27:11-07:00","id":1440613,"title":"","content":"I seem to recall that both nukes were listed as contributing to the Avatar Storm, though I'd have to check my books to be sure. Quite possibly the relic-nuke was just stated to possibly contribute with no official word actually given.<br /> <br /> As I recall, the spirit-nuke didn't even finish the job, it just cleared the cloud cover the three Bodhisattvas conjured up. The final blow was using a bunch of satellites to concentrate sunlight on the area. Outside of knowing something vampiric was going on, I don't know that the Technocracy really knew what it was dealing with. I find it very believable that they used the kitchen sink option.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T11:25:36-07:00","id":1440618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1440610#post1440610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am talking about the Avatar Storm, not the Sixth Great Maelstrom. Why would they not use a weapon designed to affect the material world, where Zapathasura actually was located? It's not plausible that they had no normal tactical nukes. Certainly they didn't expect it to hurt them, but they did design a weapon to destroy the Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>If my memory from the Week of Nigthmares isn't failing me:<br /> <br /> Zapathasura wasn't figting only in the material world, he was figthing simultaneously on more than one layer of reality: the worlds of the dead, nigthmares and demons. He and/or the Bodis had oppened doors to summon armies of evil spirits, that were rampaging over the place instead of just focusing on the figth (as seen by the local werewolves, before being obliterated by the blast themselves). This is also reported by wraiths that had to leave the premises to avoid getting sucked into the fray (which normaly wouldn't be a problem for an observer on the other side of the Shroud).<br /> <br /> What the spirit nuke does (as seen by those local werewolves), it's to merge the &quot;three worlds&quot; penumbrae into one with the material world, then do insane damage to all of it ...<br /> <br /> Judging by that: It's a weapon to use against enemies that can easily traverse and influence different layers of reality. Like powerful mages, werewolves, and even some powerful mage-vampires. You know, the kind of foe that can have an army at both sides of the Gauntlet<br /> <br /> As Ramnesis said: Technocracy had a vague idea of what was going on.<br /> <br /> They knew there were &quot;Advengers-level&quot; vampires, a &quot;demonic army&quot; of sorts, and some clouds that were resistant to magical attempts to remove them.<br /> <br /> I think it's reasonable to think the spirit nukes were used instead of normal ones to kill the hostiles, because these would have greater effect on enemies that weren't solely from Earth, and migth not be limited to exist only on Earth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Storm was caused by regular non-Nephandi VEs dropping a spirit nuke (not a normal nuke) on Bangladesh. I'm skeptical that a soul-nuke designed to obliterate entire layers of the Umbra &quot;accidentally&quot; did precisely that. </div> </div> </div>The storm was caused by three disjointed and simultaneous events. The spirit nuke, the 6th Maelstrom, and the Horizon War. And while Technocracy has a lot of blame on all of these, I wouldn't say they did it <i>on purpose</i>.<br /> <br /> As per Revised Storitellers Handbook, p 34:<br /> Avatar storm: Why it happened. First, it was a logical result of nuclear weapons going in the Underworld and Doissetep exploding in the Umbra. Second...goes on to explain meta reasons.<br /> <br /> Notably, the ppl that <i>invented </i>the storm does not mention Ravnos incident when trying to justify their decision (not here, nor in the FAQ when they talk about the Storm), albeit I'm almost sure that get's mentioned in other books as part of the cause (but I can't remember were, so IDK). <hr /><br /> The Avatar Storm it's formed by the shards of countless shattered Avatars. A good question would be: Where did those come from? An Avatar doesn't just &quot;shatter&quot; when you kill people, to shatter an Avatar, inordinate amounts of suffering or magical power needs to be employed.<br /> <br /> *One of the big casualties of the Horizon War was Doissetep. This chantry was inhabited by powerful Masters &amp; Archmasterts that were constantly conspirating against each other, when the chantry suffered a surprise attack by the technocracy, a lot of these died. Problem is, powerful mages don't just &quot;die&quot; - they tend to have curses and spells placed to be released at the moment of death. A chain reaction of post-mortem Archmaster curses caused the extremely potent explosion of the Chantry, that took out nearby Realms, and also damaged the entirety of the Digital Web(killing the VA that were immersed there). This kind of things can shatter an Avatar.<br /> <br /> *The Spirit Nuke also killed many, and certainly does seem like it has the powah to shatter Avatars, but most ppl there were already dead. Perhaps that's why it isn't mentioned in the ST handbook. Still I think it was mentioned elsewhere...but I only have vague memories of why Ravnos was important<br /> <br /> But it's not enough to shatter a lot of Avatars, in order to make such a large Storm. The 6th Maelstrom apparently acted like an &quot;engine&quot; to push the Avatars into motion. How does this work? heck if I know, but that the phenomena are connected it's a constant in all books where the Storm it's talked about seriously and off character.<br /> <br /> While all of these events have Technocracy at it's center, at most, one could accuse them of lack of foresight and wisdom. Of having the Hubris of making such weapons and such harsh judgements in the first place. Of thinking they would be able to do mass murder w/o consequences &quot;for the greater good&quot;.<br /> <br /> But that's not the same as saying they were planing for it, at least not that we know. That would have been stupid, the Technocracy was the most affected faction by far (as I remember somone said somewhere: &quot;Traditionalists had already been defeated at the Horizon War, the Storm just returned the love to the Technocracy&quot;). Also, it would defeat the purpose of the War (why go all the way there to kill the mages, if you plan to unleash a Storm that would do the same? Surely there were easier targets to get the Avatar shards from...)<br /> <br /> And about the Storm as Paradox argument - that sounds more like poetry than fact. Yeah, it was a punishment for the Hubris of mages in general, and the Technocracy in particular - like Paradox - but it's not like Paradox it's the <i>only</i> punishment for Hubris.<br /> <br /> In general the point of Hubris, it's that taking those courses of action punishes itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-19-2021, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T13:16:00-07:00","id":1440627,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the actions of [Ravnos] and Wan Kuei Bodhisattva during the Weeks of Nightmares were utterly destructive. The Technocracy didn't just decide they were going to nuke them. They sent a number of combat teams to the fight but they only lasted for moments such was the destructive power of the battle. Them declaring for the first and so far only time, Operation Ragnarok was a sign of just how desperate the situation was. Ragnarok is their final contingency, when all other attempts have failed and the situation is so world-threatening, the Technocracy is willing to use their Hypertechnology Superweapons on Earth in a last desperate attempt to save the world.<br /> <br /> And the thing is, if they hadn't we'd have no idea how the situation would have ended. Yeah their actions contributed to the 6GM and the AV but if they hadn't, [Ravnos] would have rampaged on longer and caused more damage. Hell, it's entirely possible that the Bodhisattva would not have been able to defeat him. What then? What do we about the rampaging Ante? Worse, what if he comes to his senses and we have an aware Ante active on the planet?<br /> <br /> In that regard, the Technocracy didn't really have a choice. It was either risk using these superweapons on Earth or allow this rampage to continue for who knows how long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T18:57:48-07:00","id":1440672,"title":"","content":"Well the Technocracy didn't cause the Avatar Storm.<br /> <br /> A Nephandi Void Engineer dropping a nuke in the Labyrinth did, which is attempting to NUKE HELL.<br /> <br /> The Antediluvian just showed the Union had been missing globe-threatening reality deviants in their petty war with a bunch of spoon benders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T20:16:15-07:00","id":1440679,"title":"","content":"Actually Jones wasn't Nephandi, he was potentially rogue, potentially undercover in the Orphic Circle. He also didn't drop a nuke on the Labyrinth (or at least didn't get the chance to) and that did not cause the Avatar Storm. That caused the Sixth Great Maelstrom, which itself was by the Smiling Lord dropping a relic nuke on Enoch in the Shadowlands, with the shockwave of said nuke causing Jones' nuke to go off as he was traveling the Labyrinth.<br /> <br /> And the Stygian invasion of Enoch that lead to said nuking was itself arranged by the Ferrymen at the behest of the God Anubis whom ages ago had stuck a deal with them with the intent to cause the 6GM to awaken Osiris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T00:41:26-07:00","id":1440691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1440627#post1440627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the thing is, if they hadn't we'd have no idea how the situation would have ended. Yeah their actions contributed to the 6GM and the AV but if they hadn't, [Ravnos] would have rampaged on longer and caused more damage. Hell, it's entirely possible that the Bodhisattva would not have been able to defeat him. What then? What do we about the rampaging Ante? Worse, what if he comes to his senses and we have an aware Ante active on the planet?<br /> <br /> In that regard, the Technocracy didn't really have a choice. It was either risk using these superweapons on Earth or allow this rampage to continue for who knows how long.</div> </div> </div> </div>We know how the situation was <i>supposed</i> to end from the Dharma books - the bodhisattvas would have defeated [Ravnos]. Of course, we don't know what the other consequences of that would've been.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T04:12:16-07:00","id":1440705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1440691#post1440691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We know how the situation was <i>supposed</i> to end from the Dharma books - the bodhisattvas would have defeated [Ravnos]. Of course, we don't know what the other consequences of that would've been.</div> </div> </div> </div>I choose to believe mindless Ravnos would have beaten them but I admit to have a lingering belief the Kuei Jin were Worf Effecting everyone.<br /> <br /> Everyone else was being forced to play Jobber to them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T07:31:05-07:00","id":1440713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1440691#post1440691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We know how the situation was <i>supposed</i> to end from the Dharma books - the bodhisattvas would have defeated [Ravnos]. Of course, we don't know what the other consequences of that would've been.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could I get a book and page number on that because I don't recall that and my quick searches have only brought up the character entries on the three Bodhisattvas and I did not see anything to suggest that within those entries. The most I saw was talk of Wan Kuei speculating things about the battle but even then none of that was claiming they were definitely going to win. And even if it was, what in-universe character speculation does not make it true. By that same token, depending on where and how it is written it could be from an in-character perspective which also means it may not be true but rather what the character or group believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T06:05:31-07:00","id":1440936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek#post1439351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have another annoying question about the Technocracy. A few times I've seen them mentioned as the only option for playing hard-science Star Trek types. But...<br /> <br /> Star Trek is just about the mushiest, least consistent, least plausible scifi on TV. And The Federation is all about .... communism and the Prime Detective. It's even a multi-species collective.<br /> But the Void Engineers are capitalist space marines? Funded by the Syndicate. And... they shoot aliens instead of making alliances with them?<br /> And... isn't outer space literally in the Umbra? Doesn't that make hard sci-fi just not possible in-setting?<br /> <br /> Once again, I don't get it. Not saying it's badwrongfun, but <i>how</i> does it scratch that Star Trek itch?</div> </div> </div> </div>I always though the Federation was more Etherite than Technocrat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T06:21:13-07:00","id":1440937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AscentionTheMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1440936#post1440936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always though the Federation was more Etherite than Technocrat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. But most of the board is playing with the notion that the show is VE inspired.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T15:03:06-07:00","id":1440978,"title":"","content":"Eh, the Star Trek comes down hard on superstitious thinking. It's very preachy that science and logic is the only way, and those who disagree are preached at by the protagonists, and the protagonists are always proven right in the end. That's a very Technocrat message.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T16:42:02-07:00","id":1440988,"title":"","content":"The way I look at it:<br /> <br /> post-Anomaly VEs: Battlestar Galactica (reboot)<br /> pre-Anomaly VEs: Star Trek (pre-Abrams)<br /> Sons of Ether: Doctor Who, Star Wars, Star Trek (Abrams&amp;co.)<br /> <br /> As presented in their original Conventions Book, the Void Engineers practiced \u201cTecknology\u201d, taking advantage of the lack of any rigidity in the Umbra to go all out on force field, reactionless drives, phasers, and all the other stuff that would have been Vulgar on Earth. They still fit the Technocracy's overall philosophy, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3598_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3598\" data-vbnamecard=\"3598\">CajunKhan</a> just outlined; but their science was rather squishy \u2014 so much so that VEs visiting Earth needed to wear a device designed to alter them when what they were about to try would be Vulgar. <br /> <br /> The Revised Convention Book makes no mention of Tecknology, or of needing reminders as to what's Vulgar what what isn't. They <i>do</i> practice Hypertechnology, and tend to take it to further extremes than the other Conventions do (the opposite extreme being the Syndicate, who are so devoted to keeping everything Coincidental that others sometimes wonder if they're actually Sleepers); but these days, they keep everything as extrapolations of the Technocratic Reality Zones on Earth as much as possible, and work harder to justify how what they have <i>is</i> an advanced version of what the rest of the Union has. Though on the flip side, they're in a hot war, and can't afford to ignore a bit of Hypertechnology just because they haven't yet rationalized it. <br /> <br /> The point is that they used to play it a lot more fast and loose than they do now. Before, they were thumbing their noses at their Earth-bound associates; now, they're making an effort to work with them. <br /> <br /> Presumably, the main reason for the change is that the bulk of the ones who were threatening to jump ship were in the Umbra when the Dimensional Anomaly struck, and died, Void Adapted, or made good on their threat to leave, leaving behind the ones with Earthside assignments, a more grounded outlook, and better relations with the other Conventions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-24T14:47:45-07:00","id":1441306,"title":"","content":"thread is broken. ignore this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-24-2021, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-24T14:59:35-07:00","id":1441307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1440627#post1440627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the thing is, if they hadn't we'd have no idea how the situation would have ended.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has also been stated as a fact in the Nagah Breedbook, that the Bodhisattvas were winning and on the verge of destroying Zapathasura.<br /> <br /> The Technocracts didn't know that ... although perhaps they would have if they had paid attention to what was happening in the fight instead of just panicking. But no, I agree they didn't plan the Avatar Storm to happen.<br /> <br /> Edit: Do they realize in retrospect that murdering millions of people and destroying their souls forever made it worse?<br /> Edit: Another way of asking: Do they honestly think that killing millions of people and gilguling them &quot;saved&quot; those people from Ravana? I don't really get the impression that VEs think mass-murdering humans is OK, but the weapons they used are just insane.<br /> <br /> <br /> I thought Doissetep was destroyed in 1997. But the Avatar Storm and Sixth Great Maelstrom started in 1999, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1440988#post1440988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Presumably, the main reason for the change is that the bulk of the ones who were threatening to jump ship were in the Umbra when the Dimensional Anomaly struck, and died, Void Adapted, or made good on their threat to leave, leaving behind the ones with Earthside assignments, a more grounded outlook, and better relations with the other Conventions.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they left where did they go? Just out into the Dark Umbra, or what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-24-2021, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-24T17:24:44-07:00","id":1441325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441307#post1441307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has also been stated as a fact in the Nagah Breedbook, that the Bodhisattvas were winning and on the verge of destroying Zapathasura.<br /> <br /> The Technocracts didn't know that ... although perhaps they would have if they had paid attention to what was happening in the fight instead of just panicking. But no, I agree they didn't plan the Avatar Storm to happen. They still designed weapons to mass-gilgul millions or billions of people, or to break the universe. There's no definition of &quot;greater good&quot; that includes doing that.<br /> <br /> Do they even recognize in retrospect that murdering millions of people and destroying their souls forever made it worse?</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not have that book so I cannot comment on that. However it depends on how that material was presented because if it was presented from an in-universe perspective that doesn't necessarily make it true just want that person or group believes.<br /> <br /> As for the Technocrats knowing, they couldn't. As I said, all their teams being sent were getting rapidly killed while their spy satellites could not penetrate the dark clouds summoned to block the sun. They were largely blind as an apocalyptic battle was going on between vampires that were wielding unprecedented power. Like I said, their only option was to either do nothing which they couldn't really do or use their last resort.<br /> <br /> As for the death toll, in Time of Thin-Blood where we see these events and get actual numbers, the mortal losses are estimated to be around 1.3 million people. Most of those however were caused by [Ravnos] and his rampage. Those killed by Technocrat weapons are around 60,800 people. More people were killed by the storm that was summoned to block out the sun, around 115,600 people. Because the storm wasn't just storm cloud overhead but a typhoon slamming into Bangladesh.<br /> <br /> This was not just some blast'em all and forget move. This was the cold calculus of the battlefield. To sacrifice some lives to save more. Plenty of Technocrats died right up til the nukes dropped. One of the PoVs of those events we get is a Garou who's pack has become swept up in the battle. His pack stumbles on a team of Technocracts that were wiped out by the rampaging demons that came with [Ravnos] (though whether they were true demons or products of his Chemisty mastery is up for debate) while setting up a device of some kind. While we and the Garou have no idea what exactly those devices are, the Garou thinks that it's either part of something to harm [Ravnos] or something to help contain the damage of the weapons they were about to use. Given the nukes and mirrors they used were launched from satellites, that means that said devices were either some kind of targeting device to help them focus their weapons upon [Ravnos] rather than fire blindly into the storm or a shield device to contain the worst of the damage. Either way, the Technocray was taking steps to minimize the damage they were about to do.<br /> <br /> If you're going to blame the Technocracy for what happened, you have to blame everyone else involved as well because they were not solely responsible for the deaths caused by the Week of Nightmares. Nor did they cause the most deaths of the people there.<br /> <br /> As for the Wraiths and Spirits of the region, they were being driven mad by the whole thing before the nukes fell. In fact that aforementioned Garou pack met it's end fighting against hordes of insane ghosts as a nuke fell on them. [Ravnos], it's rampage and the battle had scarred the Umbra and the Underworld. It's debatable if the Fera could have healed the damage caused to the Umbra and the Spirits but they wouldn't be able to do anything for the Wraiths and there's no telling what kind of harm those insane ghosts could have done. <br /> <br /> So yeah, it's difficult question to answer. Do you wipe out these insane spirits and ghosts that will cause harm on their own as well or do you hold back on the vague hope that the Fera and/or Mages <i>might</i> be able to heal them eventually? <br /> <br /> Of course that's not factoring in the rational, cold calculus of battle which the Technocracy was running on with the WoN. Because again, as they saw the situation it was sacrificing the lives of some (including their own) to preserve many, many more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-24T18:15:41-07:00","id":1441329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441307#post1441307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has also been stated as a fact in the Nagah Breedbook, that the Bodhisattvas were winning and on the verge of destroying Zapathasura.</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify: Dragon wizard seers assured the Nagah, after the fact, that if the Technocracy hadn't intervened, one of the \u201cChinese demons\u201d would have prevailed. That assurance is exactly as reliable as the seers are. As well, the information provided by then only details who the eventual winner would have been; there was nothing about what the cost would have been. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441307#post1441307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Technocracts didn't know that ... although perhaps they would have if they had paid attention to what was happening in the fight instead of just panicking. But no, I agree they didn't plan the Avatar Storm to happen.<br /> <br /> Edit: Do they realize in retrospect that murdering millions of people and destroying their souls forever made it worse?<br /> Edit: Another way of asking: Do they honestly think that killing millions of people and gilguling them &amp;quot;saved&amp;quot; those people from Ravana? I don't really get the impression that VEs think mass-murdering humans is OK, but the weapons they used are just insane.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Nagah Breedbook says nothing about what the Technocracy knew or didn't know, what their motives were, or anything else about them for that matter: indeed, they're not even referred to as the Technocracy; they're referred to as an unknown third party. Even the Void Engineers Convention Book doesn't do much to fill in the details; it has a paragraph about how they dropped bombs and turned orbital mirrors on the surface of the Earth in response to the rise of \u201can entity out of legend\u201d. But let me suggest a couple of thoughts: <br /> <br /> 1. You're saying that the bombs gilguled millions. As far as I know, no: they devastated the Penumbra, which was being flooded by spirits from the various layers of the Umbra after the Gauntlet and Shroud had been shredded by [Ravnos]; but there's no evidence that any Avatars were damaged. Avatars are not spirits; and they don't exist independently in the Umbra. <br /> <br /> 2. The Nagah Breedbook compares the bombs to Hiroshima and Nagasaki, and I think it's an apt comparison: but the <i>full</i> comparison is that the WWII projections were that without the bombs, the more conventional invasion of Japan would have resulted in at least twice as many casualties, and would likely have completely devastated Japan. As sad as it is to say, those bombings arguably <i>saved</i> lives overall. Which is not to say that they weren't horrendous; they were. In the same way, the people who were killed by the Technocracy's bombs would almost certainly have died anyway, what with godlike monsters fighting, demonic storms raging, and more prosaic monsters flooding in from the Umbra and Underworld after [Ravnos] shredded the Gauntlet and the Shroud. The Technocracy didn't save any of <i>their</i> lives; but they likely <i>did</i> save many lives that would have been lost had the battle raged on. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441307#post1441307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought Doissetep was destroyed in 1997. But the Avatar Storm and Sixth Great Maelstrom started in 1999, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. The destruction of the Horizon Realms was an ongoing process that had been going on for some time before the Avatar Storm struck. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441307#post1441307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they left where did they go? Just out into the Dark Umbra, or what?</div> </div> </div> </div>Out into the Deep Umbra, yes; to find whatever's out there. Recall again my supposition earlier in this thread that there may be other worlds out there, and the Deep Umbra is the expanse that you must cross to reach them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-24T21:09:06-07:00","id":1441345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441329#post1441329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify: Dragon wizard seers assured the Nagah, after the fact, that if the Technocracy hadn't intervened, one of the \u201cChinese demons\u201d would have prevailed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that doesn't look reliable.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441325#post1441325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the death toll, in Time of Thin-Blood where we see these events and get actual numbers, the mortal losses are estimated to be around 1.3 million people. Most of those however were caused by [Ravnos] and his rampage. Those killed by Technocrat weapons are around 60,800 people. More people were killed by the storm that was summoned to block out the sun, around 115,600 people. Because the storm wasn't just storm cloud overhead but a typhoon slamming into Bangladesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is helpful information, and not something available in the books I have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441325#post1441325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Either way, the Technocray was taking steps to minimize the damage they were about to do.<br /> <br /> If you're going to blame the Technocracy for what happened, you have to blame everyone else involved as well because they were not solely responsible for the deaths caused by the Week of Nightmares. Nor did they cause the most deaths of the people there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't love the Gui-Ren any more after learning that they decided to kill all those people with a hurricane, when they could have at least tried to accomplish the same goal with a cloud of darkness, or just attacked from the Umbra or Underworld where the sun never shines.<br /> <br /> I don't know what weapons of mass destruction were used by the others attacking Ravana. I'm not aware of non-Ratkin shapeshifters or changelings having such weapons, actually. Other shifters can cause local, relatively small storms. Or local bursts of sunlight that only hurt vampires. I don't think their magic can blow up entire cities worth of people. They can call on spirits and <i>ask</i> them to destroy a target.<br /> <br /> <br /> I was going to say that I can't blame people for making horrible decisions when panicked, and it happens a lot in tragedy. But coldly deciding to sacrifice an obscene number of civilians is different. I have spent my life watching politicians callously sacrifice tens of thousands, hundreds of thousands, and millions of lives for vaguely justified benefits that never actually seem to help anyone but themselves. I have had to fear more than once that I would be &quot;sacrificed&quot;. I just can't accept a version of the greater &quot;good&quot; in which tens of thousands or millions of human (or any sapient) lives are decreed worthless, for anyone's benefit. It's as awful as killing people for their organs. I'd rather die than murder someone to harvest their organs for myself.<br /> <br /> No, I don't accept the American claim that nuking Japanese civilians was right. I won't go on a side-track about purely real world events. But neither American generals nor the Void Engineers could actually know that they would save more lives than they destroyed. It's just a <i>game</i> of spitballing vague estimates and deciding which people are <b>worth</b> more than others. Both were also screwing around with vast, cosmic forces they didn't understand. And I can't ignore that in both cases, wealthy Westerners decided to sacrifice an obscene number of Asian* lives. I just cannot really trust their judgment that they &quot;had&quot; to do it.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the World of Darkness there are also fates much, <b>much</b> worse than death. Gilgul is one. You say the Technocrats' bombs didn't gilgul all those people. OK. So then....who did design (well before the battle) the magic which tore apart &quot;countless&quot; Avatars into jagged shards that then went on to gilgul countless more random people? Who decided that was an acceptable risk? Or who screwed around with the cosmic forces that could do that, without bothering to learn enough to know what the consequences would be? Was it the Relic nukes in the Underworld?<br /> <br /> <br /> *I know &quot;Asian&quot; is a very, very broad 'category'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441329#post1441329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct. The destruction of the Horizon Realms was an ongoing process that had been going on for some time before the Avatar Storm struck.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had thought that the Horizon War and blowing up Doissetep were purely the result of pointless civil wars within and between Traditions. But if they were both destroyed by Technocrats attacking -- that's another example insane world-destroying magic, da** the cosmic consequences, and for vastly less &quot;justification&quot;. Although I imagine it was multiple Conventions, not only the Void Engineers, right?<br /> <br /> Plus destroying all those Bygone and mundane endangered species living in Horizon Realms, after they'd already been being eradicated everywhere else. How many entire species went extinct?<br /> <br /> I don't know if that's worse than when some Technocrats let the Nephandi take over the whole Mercury system, just to take it out of Tradition hands. Was that the VEs or another Convention? If it was the VEs that looks pretty out of character with how they're described in 2E. To make a Star Trek analogy, I think the Federation would even try to work with the Dominion rather than just hand an inhabited Dominion planet (or moon) to the Borg. Not even the Order of Hermes are nearly as bad as the Nephandi.<br /> <br /> It's just... very hard for me to believe the (non-VE) Technocratic claim that all Mystick Mages and all the sleeper cultures who believe in their magic must be genocided utterly to the last because <b>they're</b> the irresponsible ones. The Himalayan War and Dragon River War were certainly insanely destructive and unjustifiable, but ... less so than blowing up entire worlds in retaliation. Less destructive than the results of industrialization (which, in the WoD, is actually destroying the whole Earth and Middle Umbra, not 'just' the biosphere). Also those Mystick wars ended many centuries ago. Are there more recent examples of Mysticks causing cosmic mass destruction? Were they equally responsible for Doissetep blowing up? I'm honestly asking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":".  spelling 03-25-2021, 12:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-24T22:39:24-07:00","id":1441351,"title":"","content":"No one knows where the Avatar shards came from, or why. In <b>Ascension</b>, there's a suggestion that when the Reckoning happened, Avatar shards started pouring into the Umbra toward Earth from wherever Avatars go between incarnations, in connection with the Red Star that manifested around the same time. There's no indication that anything anyone did caused Avatars to be stripped out of people and shattered. For all we know, the shards were incomplete Avatars that had been released from wherever they come from before they were ready.<br /> <br /> And yeah; in an ideal world, it would be great if you could save lives without ever having to lose any. The <i>real</i> world isn't ideal, let alone the World of <i>Darkness</i>. I'm not going to praise anyone for sacrificing innocent lives in the quest to save others; but I'm not going to automatically condemn them, either. And far more often than I'd like, the best you can do is to make the least bad choice available to you. There's a reason they're called <i>hard choices</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-25T10:24:40-07:00","id":1441389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441345#post1441345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I don't love the Gui-Ren any more after learning that they decided to kill all those people with a hurricane, when they could have at least tried to accomplish the same goal with a cloud of darkness, or just attacked from the Umbra or Underworld where the sun never shines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Elder Wan-Kuei are pretty divorced from human mortality by default due to how one becomes a Bodhisattva. In fact, while we don't get their PoV or really for that matter the fight itself, the Wan-Kuei PoV is presented through another one who's observing the fight from afar with her disciplines and... well he's only ever referred to as a 'serpent-man' but it's implied he's a Changeling (a Fu Hsi) rather than a Fera as the pair seem too friendly with one another for him to be a Fera. Oh and he too is helping out with the storm as as one she asks him to strengthen the clouds over them.<br /> <br /> And she actually says the following about the battle shortly before noticing the Technocracy attempting to part the storm clouds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;It is the Yomi World,&quot; Tieh Ju explained to the curious snake-man. &quot;Hell on Earth. If nothing contains it soon, it will cover the world. In opening doors to both the Yin and Yang Worlds, the Bodhisattvas may have acted imprudently.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Tieh Ju was likely an Ancestor or Mandarin with it's presented. Given that, her comment about it does not exactly bode well for the fight. That's not something one says if their side is winning. In fact, it comes across as the Bodhisattvas acting desperately and perhaps cause their own share of damage to the Umbra and Underworld in that desperation. That even if they do win in the end, the damaged caused by it may be too great. So yeah that's not a good sign for what was going on.<br /> <br /> Again this was an <u><i><b>APOCALYPTIC </b></i></u> battle going on. Ravnos, Psychics, Seers, and certainly mentally ill people felt through the days and nights it happened. It haunted the dreams of everyone and for some it followed them into the waking world, giving mortal and supernatural alike momentary madness. We saw of the damage that was causing, from patients of mental hospitals going berserk, harming themselves or others, to one hysterical psychic girl getting arrested and inadvertently spreading the delusions to the station, resulting in the deaths of two officers. And that's just what we got a glimpse of. The local Umbra and Underworld were being just as ravaged as the Earth was. Ghosts and spirits in the area were being driven mad. And as Tieh Ju pointed out, if it was only going to get worse.<br /> <br /> It was called a Preview of Gehenna for good reason. This was the event that kick off the march to the Time of Judgement, the end of original of the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know what weapons of mass destruction were used by the others attacking Ravana. I'm not aware of non-Ratkin shapeshifters or changelings having such weapons, actually. Other shifters can cause local, relatively small storms. Or local bursts of sunlight that only hurt vampires. I don't think their magic can blow up entire cities worth of people. They can call on spirits and <i>ask</i> them to destroy a target. </div> </div> </div>Oh they can cause mass destruction in their own ways. As I said, the typhoon was the product the Wan-Kuei and their allies. We also do know it started during Night Three of the WoN, probably at the end of the night (local time) to protect them from the sun. [Ravnos] died at the end of Night Four. So yeah they were hitting Bangladesh with a typhoon for around 24 hours. And none of them expressed any concern about the mortals they were harming.<br /> <br /> And there was actually two storms, one on Earth and another in the Umbra as alluded to above, one that was caused as result the storm they created.<br /> <br /> In fact there were only two PoVs on the battle that expressed any concern for mortals or dread about the harm to mortals they were causing the Garou pack and the Technocrat overseeing their operations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was going to say that I can't blame people for making horrible decisions when panicked, and it happens a lot in tragedy. But coldly deciding to sacrifice an obscene number of civilians is different. I have spent my life watching politicians callously sacrifice tens of thousands, hundreds of thousands, and millions of lives for vaguely justified benefits that never actually seem to help anyone but themselves. I have had to fear more than once that I would be &quot;sacrificed&quot;. I just can't accept a version of the greater &quot;good&quot; in which tens of thousands or millions of human (or any sapient) lives are decreed worthless, for anyone's benefit. It's as awful as killing people for their organs. I'd rather die than murder someone to harvest their organs for myself. </div> </div> </div>Except the thing is it wasn't a cold decision. In fact, dropping the nukes was a last resort. Noticing how above I mentioned that the Technocracy was 'attempting to part the storm clouds' because they were. They wanted to burn [Ravnos] with their orbital mirrors but they couldn't get through the clouds. In fact when Tieh Ju and her Hsien companion noticed their attempts (and she did recognize who they were) to disperse the clouds they pooled their efforts together to strengthen the clouds.<br /> <br /> Dropping the nukes to disperse the clouds was their last option. And as mentioned above, the Technocrat who declared Ragnarok and ordered the nukes to be dropped hesitated, he dreaded what he was about to do. He did not just declare these people worthless and wipe them because he saw them as less than human. Nor did it have anything to do with race as if it was happening in North America or Europe he still would have done it.<br /> <br /> Because again, Apocalyptic Battle that was the start of the Countdown to the End of the World or at least what seemed like it at the time. And this Technocrat had two bad choices, either drop the bombs and kill whatever mortals are left in the area alongside [Ravnos] or do nothing and let the rampage continue to an uncertain end eventually. He chose the less bad option because while it would kill more people, it would be far less dead than if [Ravnos] was allowed to continue.<br /> <br /> What you do in his place? Personally, I'd would have done the same thing because it was the least terrible option available to me.<br /> <br /> Before you say something about knowing the Wan-Kuei would win because of material in other books, he wouldn't know that and by extension you in his shoes wouldn't know that. And the truth is, we the players don't even know if that's true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the World of Darkness there are also fates much, <b>much</b> worse than death. Gilgul is one. You say the Technocrats' bombs didn't gilgul all those people. OK. So then....who did design (well before the battle) the magic which tore apart &quot;countless&quot; Avatars into jagged shards that then went on to gilgul countless more random people? Who decided that was an acceptable risk? Or who screwed around with the cosmic forces that could do that, without bothering to learn enough to know what the consequences would be? Was it the Relic nukes in the Underworld? </div> </div> </div>What? What are you talking about? We don't know if the weapons they used caused Gilguls. Again, while the events of the WoN (which <i>again</i> extents beyond just the use of the nukes) helped cause both the 6GM and the AS, it was not the spark that ignited those things. Had the sparks not happened, those events wouldn't have happened.<br /> <br /> As for the consequences, yet again this was a last resort scenario we're talking about. We see the protocols of Ragnarok after it's declared and just how serious it is.<br /> <br /> Operations Budget: Unlimited<br /> Permissible Weapons: Unlimited<br /> Permissible Casualties:<br /> Local Inhabitants: 100%<br /> Associate Personnel: 100%<br /> Enlightened Operatives: 100%<br /> <br /> Ragnarok is the protocol for the Worst Case Scenarios, where they're looking at potentially world-ending disasters and as a result it must be stopped no matter the cost.<br /> <br /> The Week of Nightmares was the only time they ever declared Ragnarok. That alone should tell anyone how serious this was, that the Technocracy would pull out all the stops to end, damn the consequences because that is far outside their normal operating procedures on Earth.<br /> <br /> Because the Week of Nightmares was just some fight between ancient vampires, it was a battle of unparalleled destructive power that wasn't just affecting Bangladesh but the entire planet. A battle that could have spiraled into the end of the world in it's own right. Which I think is something that people tend to forget about. They think about the Avatar Storm and the Sixth Maelstrom for what they did but treat the Week of Nightmares as a... warm up act. And on the surface, I get it. We got Ends of Empire where we're waist deep in the 6GM and it helped cause the Rev Ed lines of HtR, DtF, MtR and Orpheus. While the Avatar Storm dominated the Rev Ed for Mage and continues to be a major aspect of it. The WoN on the other hand was a brief affair that we only ever saw from afar.<br /> <br /> But as you can see from what I've talked about, it was a serious and destructive event that pretty much put the entire supernatural side of the WoD on notice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's just... very hard for me to believe the (non-VE) Technocratic claim that all Mystick Mages and all the sleeper cultures who believe in their magic must be genocided utterly to the last because <b>they're</b> the irresponsible ones. The Himalayan War and Dragon River War were certainly insanely destructive and unjustifiable, but ... less so than blowing up entire worlds in retaliation. Less destructive than the results of industrialization (which, in the WoD, is actually destroying the whole Earth and Middle Umbra, not 'just' the biosphere). Also those Mystick wars ended many centuries ago. Are there more recent examples of Mysticks causing cosmic mass destruction? Were they equally responsible for Doissetep blowing up? I'm honestly asking. </div> </div> </div>Well the VE are kind of forgetting/omitting the misdeeds of their ancestors (or outright shifting all blame to everyone else) because one of their predecessors, the Void Seekers did do some bad things in earlier times. Including attacking African Technomancers who's beliefs weren't incompatible with the Order of Reason's and stealing some of their stuff. An act that outraged members of other Conventions, both for attacking like minded Technomancers but also for doing so without consulting anyone else.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy can really be summed up as 'The Road to Hell is paved with Good Intentions' because that's really what happened. The Order of Reason started with noble intentions, to protect the Sleepers from the abuses of Mages, Supernaturals and Bygones of the time, and to elevate them. They wanted to create a world free of the monsters that preyed on Mankind, where the Arts of Man, not Magick could achieve Wonders.<br /> <br /> In fact, Mistridge, the first shots of the Ascension War, was Hermetic Chantry that had become particularly corrupt and decedent, using and abusing the local peasants for their own whims. And the rest of the OoH knew that but didn't really care. Hell, they didn't even care when it was destroyed. Some were even happy that the Craftmasons saved them the trouble of potentially having to deal with them eventually.<br /> <br /> But then their growing success and power corrupted them, and they lost sight of their noble intentions. They destroyed the Craftmasons, the Convention that very much was the soul of the Order and were the strongest advocates of the Common Man among them. By the Victorian Era they had become the very thing the Craftmasons first fought against and what they brought the others together to oppose. They became advocates of Imperialism and 'Scientific' Racism because it benefited them and the spreading of their Consensus. Where they were once at times willing to speak with their Tradition rivals, they now see them as nothing more than the enemy standing in the way of the Ordered Reality they wish to create.<br /> <br /> Because Power corrupts.<br /> <br /> And yet even with how far they've fallen, there are people within the Union that see how far it's fallen and fighting to fix it, groups like the Friends of Courage and the Harbingers of Avalon. Men and women who are fighting to right the Union's course and bring it back to the noble ideals it was founded upon.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-25T11:51:31-07:00","id":1441404,"title":"","content":"A couple of additional thoughts: The Syndicate is also not particularly interested in killing anyone. Dead people don't buy products. The revised edition also brought an end to the Pogrom, and M20 leaves it up to the Storyteller whether or not that stuck. So it's entirely within the \u201ccanon\u201d of the game too have a Technocracy that isn't out for blood. <br /> <br /> So even with \u201cthe road to hell is paved with good intentions\u201d, they're not nearly as far down that road as earlier editions depicted. Which is not to say that they're the good guys, though they certainly think they are. <br /> <br /> And yes, there are many within the Union's rank who realize that there's a problem. When it was first introduced, the Harbingers of Avalon numbered maybe a dozen total; in M20, it's mentioned that their numbers have swelled, and they're half a step away from leaving the Union to form a new Craft. And the Disparate Alliance section has an entry in its potential future allies section for Navalon, a Craft of former Technocrats who despise the corruption in the Union.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-25T13:19:30-07:00","id":1441413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441404#post1441404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple of additional thoughts: The Syndicate is also not particularly interested in killing anyone. Dead people don't buy products.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because they think they can neuter those cultures, bastardizing their beliefs so they don't get to be used as a Focus.<br /> <br /> It IS less horrible than the Pogrom propper. It's still pretty bad","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-25-2021, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-25T13:48:07-07:00","id":1441417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441345#post1441345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I don't accept the American claim that nuking Japanese civilians was right. I won't go on a side-track about purely real world events. But neither American generals nor the Void Engineers could actually know that they would save more lives than they destroyed. It's just a <i>game</i> of spitballing vague estimates and deciding which people are <b>worth</b> more than others. Both were also screwing around with vast, cosmic forces they didn't understand. And I can't ignore that in both cases, wealthy Westerners decided to sacrifice an obscene number of Asian* lives. I just cannot really trust their judgment that they &quot;had&quot; to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the difficulty is that much of the Technocracy is riffing on the self-justifying idea of the tough men making tough decisions because no one else has the guts to make them. In the real world that argument only really gets invoked when people are doing something either bad or self-serving. To use your example, it seems fairly well settled history now that the stuff about saving lives with the atomic bomb was a post hoc justification (after all, saying you used atomic bombs in a failed attempt to force a surrender before the Soviets joined the war isn't terribly flattering).<br /> <br /> Now, that more or less works for Ascension itself, but runs into trouble when you introduce existential threats from semi-separate settings like Ravana. Yeah, the guy authorising Ragnorok is pretty clearly not a great guy; but the scenario clearly does justify something like what he does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-25T14:47:30-07:00","id":1441420,"title":"","content":"I think them *having* spirit nukes could be objectionable, and certainly one couldn't have been stolen if they hadn't made them ... but the way they were used by the Technocracy ain't so easy to object<br /> <br /> As stated: It was either watch the world burn, or do something big. Perhaps they could've done something else, but we don't know and they seemed to believe it was the only option after trying many other things. So, there's that.<br /> <br /> On a color note: Star Trek: Discovery has a chapter about this. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441351#post1441351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one knows where the Avatar shards came from, or why. In <b>Ascension</b>, there's a suggestion that when the Reckoning happened, Avatar shards started pouring into the Umbra toward Earth from wherever Avatars go between incarnations, in connection with the Red Star that manifested around the same time. There's no indication that anything anyone did caused Avatars to be stripped out of people and shattered. For all we know, the shards were incomplete Avatars that had been released from wherever they come from before they were ready.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hum...I've done some research, and I think I found out what happened. It's in Bitter Road. Should be known, that's when everything begins<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p. 110</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a result of the events in the Reckoning, several nuclear weapons of various power were detonated - some in the spirit world, some in the material...when the Sixth Great Maelstrom fired off, its force was sufficent to propel spirits across the Shrowd ... however various ghosts werent the only spirit pieces that were shoved through the Gauntlet. Raw spiritual energy surged across various domains. <b>Combined with the powers released when the Digital Web crashed, when Doissetep burned and when Concordia (Horizon) fell, too much stress was placed on the Tapestry. Pieces frayed, twisted and snapped. The jagged blasts of spritual energy literally shredded and crumpled multiple Avatars - some on Sleepers, some on others; some, perhaps, that remained free souls. </b>Given spiritual impetus by the Maelstrom and other powerful forces in motion, the howling pieces of semi-aware magical energy circled the globe</div> </div> </div> </div>Ravnos it's not mentioned here either, the spirit nukes do get a passing mention.<br /> <br /> However, it seems that the weapons and spells by themselves weren't what shattered the Avatars - the spiritual energy of the Maelstrom was the last straw that broke a universe that was already weakened thanks to the powers released by mages in the War. <i>That </i>(the universe breaking) caused Avatars to be stripped out of people and shatter (and also, possibly, shattered disembodied Avatars)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-25-2021, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-25T16:18:56-07:00","id":1441429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441413#post1441413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's because they think they can neuter those cultures, bastardizing their beliefs so they don't get to be used as a Focus.<br /> <br /> It IS less horrible than the Pogrom propper. It's still pretty bad</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's also an element of them just being tired. The Technocracy had basically been on a war footing from the point that the VAs left (which IIRC is what kicked off the Pogrom). A war footing is a terribly draining thing to maintain; and the Union had been maintaining one for decades. The rise of the Avatar Storm and the subsequent loss of Control left the field agents reassessing whether or not such a strategy was worth it; and basically, they decided that it wasn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-25T22:43:33-07:00","id":1441463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441413#post1441413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's because they think they can neuter those cultures, bastardizing their beliefs so they don't get to be used as a Focus.<br /> <br /> It IS less horrible than the Pogrom propper. It's still pretty bad</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its less horrible... by their standards. I am not sure I'd agree turning &quot;Love thy neighbor&quot; into prosperity Gospel and its knock on effects are really that clean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-25T22:48:56-07:00","id":1441464,"title":"","content":"Back when Gehenna was thought to be the end of the world, the spirit nuke seemed justified. Now that we've seen Gehenna and it's kind of...meh...it doesn't seem so justified. Dropping that nuke caused a lot of misery for a lot of people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T01:19:12-07:00","id":1441475,"title":"","content":"It only seems\u2026 meh(?) in hindsight because the world ultimately survived, without being reduced to a post-Apocalyptic wasteland. Frankly, after what Bangladesh was put through, I'm surprised that it <i>isn't</i> a smoldering wreck in the current year.<br /> <br /> And I point you back to Aleph's description of the Week of Nightmares: dropping the nuke ended the conflagration. Saying that it wasn't justified in hindsight because the conflagration ended sounds\u2026 wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-26-2021, 04:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T05:00:39-07:00","id":1441488,"title":"","content":"I don't generally look at the current WoD as one were the events of Gehenna, Apocalypse, or Ascension happened. I also don't view Mage as a game where an end of the world scenario is inevitable. Possible, yes, but not inevitable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T08:26:27-07:00","id":1441506,"title":"","content":"The NWO Convention Book started out with the following (p.12): <br /> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">In another reality, the Time of Judgment came, a Red Star its herald. The world ended, either through mass Ascension, war, or catastrophe. Yet, here we are in 2012, our world for the moment still spinning. For us, the Red Star was not a harbinger of doom, but a passing moment of curiosity, is selling dread in those most paranoid. Our destinies certainly changed, and we can only hope for the better.<br /> <br /> The world didn't get off scot-free, though. The Avatar Storm continues to savage the Horizon Realms, cutting the Traditions and Technocrats alike off from their leadership. Some of these possible fates from that other reality hover over ours like the Sword of Damocles, particularly a Technocratic Civil War. as for the rest of the details in the Time of Judgment, such as the Rogue Council and the Panopticon, maybe they're in your chronicle's future. According to one school of thought, \u201cJudgment Day is inevitable\u201d. But another says there is no fate but what we make.</span></div><br /> In effect, the (last four) Revised Convention Books rolled back the end-of-the-world scenario to shortly before the rise of the Rogue Council and the Panopticon, and charts a different course from there which at least postpones the end of the world and possibly bypasses it. <br /> <br /> And that was <i>before</i> M20 rolled out and established its own \u201cthis is <i>your</i> game; do what you will\u201d mantra, providing tools to use M20 as a continuation from the Revised Convention Books, as a continuation of the 2e material, or something else entirely. The closest thing <i>it</i> has to a \u201cmetaplot development\u201d is to plant suggestions of what Brucato intended to do if not for the aim of the book to primarily be a celebration of the previous iterations of the game. Things like the notion that the Avatar Storm happened, but mostly in the past tense, the establishment of the New Horizon Council in New Zealand with renamed Traditions, the impending restructuring of the Union and a purging of reform elements in its ranks, and the secret development of a Disparate Alliance. <br /> <br /> When I talk about \u201cwhat has happened\u201d, this is more or less what I go with; but again, M20 doesn't lock you into this the way MRev attempted to lock you into its changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T16:24:02-07:00","id":1441567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441475#post1441475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It only seems\u2026 meh(?) in hindsight because the world ultimately survived, without being reduced to a post-Apocalyptic wasteland. Frankly, after what Bangladesh was put through, I'm surprised that it <i>isn't</i> a smoldering wreck in the current year.<br /> <br /> And I point you back to Aleph's description of the Week of Nightmares: dropping the nuke ended the conflagration. Saying that it wasn't justified in hindsight because the conflagration ended sounds\u2026 wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda agree, but think you're putting it in the wrong context.<br /> <br /> Ragnorok isn't some neutral event that happened, it's a fictional event that was meant to prelude the end of the world in a story.<br /> <br /> Like, if you're playing right now, with present day history, why would you choose to keep in the story about a vampire-god rising in the late nineties?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T17:10:01-07:00","id":1441576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441567#post1441567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I kinda agree, but think you're putting it in the wrong context.<br /> <br /> Ragnorok isn't some neutral event that happened, it's a fictional event that was meant to prelude the end of the world in a story.<br /> <br /> Like, if you're playing right now, with present day history, why would you choose to keep in the story about a vampire-god rising in the late nineties?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because that appears to be what White Wolf and OPP were doing. Most see the Reckoning as something that happened while the events that followed didn't. V5 is very clearly post-WoN.<br /> <br /> And honestly I think a lot of people for years were playing in that post-1999 world. I know all my modern games have been such. It's part of the norm for us.<br /> <br /> Given that these events have also removed the leadership of the Traditions and the Technocracy, allowing for changes within both groups, for younger minds to take charge and take their groups down different paths, paths that the old Masters never would have taken because they were set in their ways.<br /> <br /> Yes, the various Willworkers have lost much because of the Avatar Storm but at the same time it's granted them new possibilities. Some would argue that's worth more than what was lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T17:23:07-07:00","id":1441577,"title":"","content":"and also because if you don't keep the Week of Nightmares in the continuity, you don't get to complain about the Technocracy doing evil and wrong things during the Week of Nightmares.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T17:39:39-07:00","id":1441581,"title":"","content":"I have had some bad days and trouble putting my thoughts in words. I can\u2019t keep up with how fast everyone else posts. This post looks angrier than I intended because I've had a monumentally shitty day.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1440988#post1440988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Revised Convention Book makes no mention of Tecknology, or of needing reminders as to what's Vulgar what what isn't. They <i>do</i> practice Hypertechnology,</div> </div> </div> </div>Are Tecknology and Hypertechnology OOC or IC words?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441389#post1441389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except the thing is it wasn't a cold decision. In fact, dropping the nukes was a last resort.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, sorry. I was confused because you or Dataweaver talked up the \u201ccold calculus of war\u201d more than once.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441389#post1441389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you do in his place? Personally, I'd would have done the same thing because it was the least terrible option available to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441351#post1441351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one knows where the Avatar shards came from, or why. In <b>Ascension</b>, there's a suggestion that when the Reckoning happened, Avatar shards started pouring into the Umbra toward Earth from wherever Avatars go between incarnations, in connection with the Red Star that manifested around the same time. There's no indication that anything anyone did caused Avatars to be stripped out of people and shattered. For all we know, the shards were incomplete Avatars that had been released from wherever they come from before they were ready.<br /> <br /> And yeah; in an ideal world, it would be great if you could save lives without ever having to lose any. The <i>real</i> world isn't ideal, let alone the World of <i>Darkness</i>. I'm not going to praise anyone for sacrificing innocent lives in the quest to save others; but I'm not going to automatically condemn them, either. And far more often than I'd like, the best you can do is to make the least bad choice available to you. There's a reason they're called <i>hard choices</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for answering.<br /> <br /> Yes, the real world gives us hard choices and the WoD is designed to make them even harder and more horrible for PCs. I still do think that SPIRIT nukes capable of maybe destroying the world? were the wrong choice. A normal bomb would have been better, if bombs were truly necessary to clear the clouds. Maybe they could have drained the hurricane\u2019s energy into <s>magickal</s> Enlighened battery Devices. Whatever their options, I think they took one of the worse ones. I can stop assuming they\u2019re automatically awful people because of it, but I'm not really comfortable calling it the right decision. Knowing that their bomb wasn't designed to [be able to] cause the worldwide mass-gilgul does make it a much smaller horror than I thought.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441389#post1441389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What? What are you talking about?</div> </div> </div> </div>Calm down! Don\u2019t assume that anything I say is sarcasm. Read my signature!<br /> We are talking about the <b>Avatar Storm.</b><br /> It is made of <b>gilguled Avatars.</b><br /> <b>Something</b> or someone gilguled them, because they sure don\u2019t come that way at birth.<br /> I asked: <b>Who or what</b> gilguled them?<br /> Dataweaver answered: Nobody knows what gilguled them. It may or may not have been the Void Engineers.<br /> The end.<br /> (Thank you, Dataweaver.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441389#post1441389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again this was an <u><i><b>APOCALYPTIC </b></i></u> battle going on. Ravnos, Psychics, Seers, and certainly mentally ill people felt through the days and nights it happened. It haunted the dreams of everyone and for some it followed them into the waking world, giving mortal and supernatural alike momentary madness. We saw of the damage that was causing, from patients of mental hospitals going berserk, harming themselves or others, to one hysterical psychic girl getting arrested and inadvertently spreading the delusions to the station, resulting in the deaths of two officers. And that's just what we got a glimpse of. The local Umbra and Underworld were being just as ravaged as the Earth was. Ghosts and spirits in the area were being driven mad. And as Tieh Ju pointed out, if it was only going to get worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish this had been mentioned outside of a Vampire-only book, ostensibly about thin-blooded vampires and dhampires, that non-Vampire players wouldn\u2019t think of reading. Werewolf books say there was a battle and a storm and some god-monster in Bangladesh, nothing at all anywhere else. No hint of anything potentially world-ending.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441389#post1441389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ragnarok is the protocol for the Worst Case Scenarios, where they're looking at potentially world-ending disasters and as a result it must be stopped no matter the cost.<br /> <br /> The Week of Nightmares was the only time they ever declared Ragnarok. That alone should tell anyone how serious this was, that the Technocracy would pull out all the stops to end, damn the consequences because that is far outside their normal operating procedures on Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the Horizon, though, blowing up a dozen entire inhabited worlds is just to prove they\u2019re right and everyone else is wrong. [/snark]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441389#post1441389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the Week of Nightmares was just some fight between ancient vampires, it was a battle of unparalleled destructive power that wasn't just affecting Bangladesh but the entire planet. A battle that could have spiraled into the end of the world in it's own right. Which I think is something that people tend to forget about. They think about the Avatar Storm and the Sixth Maelstrom for what they did but treat the Week of Nightmares as a... warm up act. And on the surface, I get it. We got Ends of Empire where we're waist deep in the 6GM and it helped cause the Rev Ed lines of HtR, DtF, MtR and Orpheus. While the Avatar Storm dominated the Rev Ed for Mage and continues to be a major aspect of it. The WoN on the other hand was a brief affair that we only ever saw from afar.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s a very good point Akatsuki. There\u2019s almost nothing about the Week of Nightmares outside of one obscure Vampire book.<br /> <br /> But most Revised lines (except Werewolf and perhaps Vampire) go on and on about the WORLD ENDING NONSTOP EXPLOSION EVERYWHERE IN THE UMBRA AND UNDERWORLD!!! It was apparently meant (at the time of writing) to be literally world-ending, too (which meant <i>nobody</i> would be saved by whatever caused it). 22 years later, the WoD hasn\u2019t ended yet because people want to keep playing these games. The storms are even explicitly optional now because the writers finally figured out that many people <b>want</b> to play games that include the Umbra and/or Underworld (<i>duh</i>).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441389#post1441389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Order of Reason started with noble intentions, to protect the Sleepers from the abuses of Mages, Supernaturals and Bygones of the time, and to elevate them. They wanted to create a world free of the monsters that preyed on Mankind,</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve said elsewhere what I think of the \u201cvirtue\u201d of a merciless, pitiless, genocidal Crusade against all \u201cmonsters\u201d everywhere no matter what they were actually doing. I\u2019ll add that declaring all nonhuman beings everywhere must die just because they must be <i>inherently </i>EEEEVIL willfully ignores the nonstop mass violence and rape and torture that <b>sleepers</b> inflict on each other every day, everywhere. But they\u2019re human sleepers, so they\u2019re allowed to be violent and dangerous. And of course the Order of Reason are above petty mortal ethics so they can do anything they want to good [Christian/atheist] sleepers, let alone other people, and they\u2019re always inherently right no matter what because [God/Jesus/Science] is on their side.<br /> <br /> But a unicorn hiding in the last old-growth forest in Europe, who runs away from the mere hint of any human.... what a monster, clearly an utterly iredeemable unspeakable evil. How dare it exist outside of peer-reviewed Linnaean taxonomy!!!11 [/sarcasm]<br /> <br /> I\u2019m <i>seriously</i> tired of genocide and maniacal frothing-at-the-mouth hatred being included in \u201cnoble intentions\u201d. This more than anything keeps me hot-blooded to argue against Technocracy apologia.<br /> <br /> Edit: Keep in mind that disabled people like me have been variously called &quot;animals&quot; and &quot;monsters&quot; and &quot;possessed&quot; throughout history and would have been classified as inhuman monstrosities to be destroyed. Many disabled children are still murdered at birth. Plus I was raised in one of those &quot;evil&quot; non-mainstream-Christian religions that many people in my country still want to eradicate. So I take this &quot;dehumanizing and killing all non-conforming people is a Good Intention&quot; a little personally. Please consider the real-world actions that correspond to the original Order of Reason's &quot;noble intentions&quot; when you try to justify them.<br /> <br /> The sadistic torture of prisoners is another thing that hits very close to home for me personally. Definitely not a &quot;noble intention&quot; either.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441404#post1441404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, there are many within the Union's rank who realize that there's a problem. When it was first introduced, the Harbingers of Avalon numbered maybe a dozen total; in M20, it's mentioned that their numbers have swelled, and they're half a step away from leaving the Union to form a new Craft. And the Disparate Alliance section has an entry in its potential future allies section for Navalon, a Craft of former Technocrats who despise the corruption in the Union.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, otherwise there'd be fewer options to play non-fascist POS scientists.<br /> <br /> What year did the Pogrom end? (I know you\u2019ve said elsewhere it was just for budget reasons, not any kind of moral qualm. Then again Revised also hammered that every Craft who didn\u2019t join the Traditions was wiped out by a newer bigger badder Pogrom, so that doesn\u2019t add up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-26-2021, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T17:45:02-07:00","id":1441582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441420#post1441420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think them *having* spirit nukes could be objectionable, and certainly one couldn't have been stolen if they hadn't made them</div> </div> </div> </div>YES exactly my point! Building those weapons wasn't a good idea in my book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441420#post1441420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, it seems that the weapons and spells by themselves weren't what shattered the Avatars - the spiritual energy of the Maelstrom was the last straw that broke a universe that was already weakened thanks to the powers released by mages in the War. <i>That </i>(the universe breaking) caused Avatars to be stripped out of people and shatter (and also, possibly, shattered disembodied Avatars)</div> </div> </div> </div>Caused, again, by the Technocrats destroying about a dozen entire worlds/Umbral Realms.<br /> <br /> I'd be happy with a Mage timeline that skipped everything after the White Out. No Horizon War, no Traditions stomped into near-oblivion, no Avatar Storm, no obliteration of all Horizon Realms. The removal of the Old Masters and Control is helpful for players, but doesn't look worth it to me. Your obnoxious overlords are gone, but you lost the War and everyone you loved is dead and everything you tried to defend was blown up and you have no safe haven anywhere on Earth or in Space. Man, not even werewolves have it that bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-26-2021, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T22:09:37-07:00","id":1441601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441581#post1441581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Tecknology and Hypertechnology OOC or IC words?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tecknology is an old, out of date word that early MtAs material to refer to the Awakened Science and Technology of the Technocracy, like how the magic of Mages has been referred to as Magick. But it was silly and honestly didn't match with the nature of the Technocracy. Enlightened Science and Hypertechnology are the terms replaced it. Enlightened Science is the umbrella term for the advanced science the Technocracy practices while Hypertechnology refers to their advanced technological devices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, the real world gives us hard choices and the WoD is designed to make them even harder and more horrible for PCs. I still do think that SPIRIT nukes capable of maybe destroying the world? were the wrong choice. A normal bomb would have been better, if bombs were truly necessary to clear the clouds. Maybe they could have drained the hurricane\u2019s energy into <s>magickal</s> Enlighened battery Devices. Whatever their options, I think they took one of the worse ones. I can stop assuming they\u2019re automatically awful people because of it, but I'm not really comfortable calling it the right decision. Knowing that their bomb wasn't designed to [be able to] cause the worldwide mass-gilgul does make it a much smaller horror than I thought. </div> </div> </div>Well first off, they were actually Hypertech Neutron bombs. The 'spirit nuke' name came from the Garou I had mentioned previously as he witnessed the first bombs hit before they killed him, what left of his pack and the hordes of insane spirits that were overwhelming them.<br /> <br /> Which brings me to my next couple of points. First off, we do not if that damage they caused was because of the bombs themselves or the situation on the grounds. As I alluded to in my previous post, the battle was wrecking havoc on Earth, the Umbra and the Underworld. The barrier between worlds have been pulled extremely thin and likely tearing in places. Actually it likely was torn given that hordes of insane spirits and ghosts were pouring in.<br /> <br /> It's entirely possible that <i>any</i> sufficiently powerful bomb could have caused the same affect with the already existing damage to the Barrier. After all, the mundane Fat Man and Little Boy caused the Fifth Great Maelstrom and the Shadowlands of Nagasaki and Hiroshima are still deeply scarred by it.<br /> <br /> Second, the storm they were trying to cut through was magical in nature. Not only had it come far too fast and sudden to be natural but before they dropped those bombs the storm in response to their efforts <i>thickened</i> because the ones maintaining were actively fighting against them. They understood that they needed more punch if they were going to disperse the clouds. If the bombs had an anti-Magic/Spirit capabilities that may be why they were used.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wish this had been mentioned outside of a Vampire-only book, ostensibly about thin-blooded vampires and dhampires, that non-Vampire players wouldn\u2019t think of reading. Werewolf books say there was a battle and a storm and some god-monster in Bangladesh, nothing at all anywhere else. No hint of anything potentially world-ending. </div> </div> </div>Likely because the main people affected by the WoN were the Vampires, both breeds of them, and to a lesser extent the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> All the Garou really know is that some big and destructive happened in the area, and the one pack they sent to investigate was wiped out there.<br /> <br /> That they added to a book on the Thin-bloods is annoying but it does make a degree of sense as they are commonly connected to the Gehenna Myths and the WoN was a sign post on the Road to Gehenna. Plus there are seers among the Thin-bloods and said seers were among those deeply affected by the WoN.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But most Revised lines (except Werewolf and perhaps Vampire) go on and on about the WORLD ENDING NONSTOP EXPLOSION EVERYWHERE IN THE UMBRA AND UNDERWORLD!!! It was apparently meant (at the time of writing) to be literally world-ending, too (which meant <i>nobody</i> would be saved by whatever caused it). 22 years later, the WoD hasn\u2019t ended yet because people want to keep playing these games. The storms are even explicitly optional now because the writers finally figured out that many people <b>want</b> to play games that include the Umbra and/or Underworld (<i>duh</i>). </div> </div> </div>Actually several options, including that the AS happened but the storm has or is in the process of abating. And even when the Storm was big and going on, there were still ways to get to the Umbra and Underworld. Hell, the VE were playing nice with Euthanatos because they control Ravana's Naval, a region in India where one could easily enter the Umbra.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I\u2019ve said elsewhere what I think of the \u201cvirtue\u201d of a merciless, pitiless, genocidal Crusade against all \u201cmonsters\u201d everywhere no matter what they were actually doing. I\u2019ll add that declaring all nonhuman beings everywhere must die just because they must be <i>inherently </i>EEEEVIL willfully ignores the nonstop mass violence and rape and torture that <b>sleepers</b> inflict on each other every day, everywhere. But they\u2019re human sleepers, so they\u2019re allowed to be violent and dangerous. And of course the Order of Reason are above petty mortal ethics so they can do anything they want to good [Christian/atheist] sleepers, let alone other people, and they\u2019re always inherently right no matter what because [God/Jesus/Science] is on their side.<br /> <br /> But a unicorn hiding in the last old-growth forest in Europe, who runs away from the mere hint of any human.... what a monster, clearly an utterly iredeemable unspeakable evil. How dare it exist outside of peer-reviewed Linnaean taxonomy!!!11 [/sarcasm]<br /> <br /> I\u2019m <i>seriously</i> tired of genocide and maniacal frothing-at-the-mouth hatred being included in \u201cnoble intentions\u201d. This more than anything keeps me hot-blooded to argue against Technocracy apologia. </div> </div> </div>Forgive me. I sometimes forget that people haven't read the same books as me and forget to add content I know that others may not.<br /> <br /> But when I say that Technocracy has fallen far and that the Order was noble, I mean it. Because you see, Mage: the Sorcerer's Crusade makes it quite clear that the Order wasn't against the Supernatural, they were against the monsters that harmed Humanity. The Supernatural wasn't something to be feared or hated but studied and understood. Because the Order of Reason itself at this time used the Supernatural as well. Back then the line between Science and Magic was much thinner. And many of the groups that founded the Order of Reason could and did trace their roots back to earlier magical groups. The Craftmasons were originally group within the Order of Hermes before they left to form their own group during the time of Dark Ages Mage. Indeed those early Craftmasons were not all that removed from their former Hermtic colleges.<br /> <br /> In fact the MtSC Rulebook even takes about how Tradition-Convention parties are possible in this era.<br /> <br /> Of course they did have their zealots and assholes (the Cabal of Pure Thought comes to mind) but then all groups have such people.<br /> <br /> Hell, in the in-universe writings of the First Cabal (the events of which would help throw fuel on the growing fire between the Order and Traditions), it's revealed that the leaders of the future Cult of Ecstasy had foreseen the Great Betrayal but allowed it to happen because they had also seen what would happen otherwise, the Traditions and Order eventually uniting into a single organization that becomes even worse than the Technocracy. Such a thing is impossible in the modern day but back then things were different. The Ascension War hadn't yet become as bitter and bloody as it would. The differences between the Order and Traditions was not as deep yet. And the Order hadn't yet fallen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: Keep in mind that disabled people like me have been variously called &quot;animals&quot; and &quot;monsters&quot; and &quot;possessed&quot; throughout history and would have been classified as inhuman monstrosities to be destroyed. Many disabled children are still murdered at birth. Plus I was raised in one of those &quot;evil&quot; non-mainstream-Christian religions that many people in my country still want to eradicate. So I take this &quot;dehumanizing and killing all non-conforming people is a Good Intention&quot; a little personally. Please consider the real-world actions that correspond to the original Order of Reason's &quot;noble intentions&quot; when you try to justify them.<br /> <br /> The sadistic torture of prisoners is another thing that hits very close to home for me personally. Definitely not a &quot;noble intention&quot; either. </div> </div> </div>True but that's more a product of the time than something specific to the Order. Because many Tradition Mages would similar beliefs. And actually there are plenty in the Order back then that would have been more likely to attempt to help such people* than many in the Traditions would because at that time (and this is part of why the Order became so successful) many in the Traditions didn't care much about the normal people. Some of the worst ones saw themselves as above the Sleepers and could rule over them however they wished. It's one of the things that made the Craftmasons stand out, their strong advocacy for the Common Man. In a time when most other Mage groups cared little for the Sleepers, the Craftmasons were fighting for them. They were very much the moral center, the soul of the Order.<br /> <br /> Then they were destroyed by their peers and we know what followed that.<br /> <br /> *Of course, that doesn't mean that their beliefs on such mental and physically disabilities or the treatments of such things would be... well pleasant as we're still talking people of the Renaissance with the notions and ideas of that era.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What year did the Pogrom end? (I know you\u2019ve said elsewhere it was just for budget reasons, not any kind of moral qualm. Then again Revised also hammered that every Craft who didn\u2019t join the Traditions was wiped out by a newer bigger badder Pogrom, so that doesn\u2019t add up. </div> </div> </div>There's no set year for when the Pogrom ended. As for the Rev Ed, one thing you do have to keep in mind is that the Rev Ed was pushing towards the end of the world as the rest of the Rev Ed was doing at the time. But in that original run we only got one Rev Ed Convention Book, It-X. The rest came out in the years before M20, after the success of V20 paved the way, to rectify that and to kind of serve as a preview for M20.<br /> <br /> Like Data said in his quote of the NWO CB, that timeline with the wiped out Crafts, the Rogue Council and the Panopticon happened in different timeline from those CBs and M20.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-27T05:31:05-07:00","id":1441630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441576#post1441576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because that appears to be what White Wolf and OPP were doing. Most see the Reckoning as something that happened while the events that followed didn't. V5 is very clearly post-WoN.<br /> <br /> And honestly I think a lot of people for years were playing in that post-1999 world. I know all my modern games have been such. It's part of the norm for us.<br /> <br /> Given that these events have also removed the leadership of the Traditions and the Technocracy, allowing for changes within both groups, for younger minds to take charge and take their groups down different paths, paths that the old Masters never would have taken because they were set in their ways.<br /> <br /> Yes, the various Willworkers have lost much because of the Avatar Storm but at the same time it's granted them new possibilities. Some would argue that's worth more than what was lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I was referring specifically to Ravana rising not the Mage-specific stuff.<br /> <br /> Like, Time of Thin Bloods was written in a context where the end was pretty obviously meant to be a real threat, and indeed it did actually end. So reading it now, it makes the Technocrats look much worse, because the End of the World was retconned away.<br /> <br /> The thing is, that's not necessarily bad, I just think you can end up with a warped picture of what the writers are trying to do, because it's an unintended consequence of restarting the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-27T08:41:14-07:00","id":1441645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441630#post1441630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, I was referring specifically to Ravana rising not the Mage-specific stuff.<br /> <br /> Like, Time of Thin Bloods was written in a context where the end was pretty obviously meant to be a real threat, and indeed it did actually end. So reading it now, it makes the Technocrats look much worse, because the End of the World was retconned away.<br /> <br /> The thing is, that's not necessarily bad, I just think you can end up with a warped picture of what the writers are trying to do, because it's an unintended consequence of restarting the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really because the WoN was again, an Apocalyptic Battle in it's own right. That it was stopped doesn't change that nor the fact that it wasn't the preview of worse things to come. That's arguing that a Hurricane isn't bad because it wasn't followed up by worse Hurricanes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-27T14:32:53-07:00","id":1441705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439351-technocrats-and-star-trek?p=1441630#post1441630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, I was referring specifically to Ravana rising not the Mage-specific stuff.<br /> <br /> Like, Time of Thin Bloods was written in a context where the end was pretty obviously meant to be a real threat, and indeed it did actually end. So reading it now, it makes the Technocrats look much worse, because the End of the World was retconned away.<br /> <br /> The thing is, that's not necessarily bad, I just think you can end up with a warped picture of what the writers are trying to do, because it's an unintended consequence of restarting the line.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Vampire still needs the nuke. Actually it probably doesn't need a nuke so much as a &quot;very big conventional bomb&quot; but the perspective that the Antedeluvians are not unbeatable blood gods is both needed by both camarilla and sabbat propaganda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-l